WEBVTT

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:21.890
﻿Today, not long after 21:50...

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:29.360
﻿The Tokyo National Institute of Microorganisms in
﻿Nishitama City was attacked by an armed group seven strong.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:35.570
﻿The armed group restrained two security
﻿guards, took the on-duty researcher captive...

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:44.120
Infiltrated the high-security lab, detonated the plastic explosives
they planted just minutes earlier, and made their escape.

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:41.030
Uno Tadayoshi

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:41.030
Police HQ Senior Superintendent

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:41.030
Odagiri Toshirou

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:41.030
Police HQ Chief Superintendent

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.790
﻿At the lab where the explosion occurred...

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:52.000
﻿An extremely dangerous bacteria was being stored inside.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.260
﻿It is speculated the armed group took it into their possession.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:56.880
﻿Dangerous bacteria?

00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:00.720
﻿The mortality rate following infection is gauged at 80%.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:03.220
﻿To date, no known cure has been found.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.350
﻿Could the bacteria have spread to the vicinity due to the explosion?

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:08.390
﻿That is not a possibility.

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:14.860
﻿Due to the magnitude of the explosion, any traces of
﻿the potential bacteria should have been incinerated.

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:16.780
﻿That's according to testimony from the lab chief himself.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:20.450
﻿What's the aim of the assailant group?

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:22.120
﻿To be determined.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:25.950
﻿However, we are exploring the possibility of bioterrorism.

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:29.920
﻿We do have a request for all of you.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:32.920
﻿To avoid an unnecessary panic...

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:36.090
﻿Only report this as a bombing incident, and...

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:40.890
﻿Refrain from mentioning bacteria or the possibility of bioterrorism.

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:45.350
﻿Does that mean you're exercising media control?

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:52.860
﻿Chief!

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:57.610
﻿The assailant group has posted their manifesto on the internet.

00:02:57.650 --> 00:02:58.780
﻿And the name of the terrorist—

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.610
﻿The Red Siamese Cats.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:06.830
﻿"We, the Red Siamese Cats, were the ones responsible for
﻿the raid on the Tokyo National Institute of Microorganisms...

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:09.290
﻿"And have obtained the killer bacteria.

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:12.500
﻿"We will commence with our next move within seven days.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:13.790
﻿"Await your demise."

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:20.220
﻿It appears they've procured the bacteria after all.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:24.300
﻿But, weren't the Red Siamese Cats eradicated ten years ago?

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:24.890
﻿Chief!

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:27.850
﻿That means the press control will be lifted, right?

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:28.810
﻿We have no choice.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:42.240
﻿And now we welcome bacteriologist Ooda Chiaki to the show.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.910
﻿Bacteriologist
University of Beika Medicine

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.910
﻿OODA CHIAKI

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:48.370
﻿Should one become infected with this bacteria, rashes
﻿and skin irritation can emerge from any part of the body.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:50.120
Really, it's becoming a serious case.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:52.580
They've been reporting the same news since this morning.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:54.380
﻿The symptoms remain for a number of days, 
followed by prostration and possibly even death.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:58.590
﻿﻿Transmission is primarily done by droplet contact.

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:02.760
﻿﻿Young children are especially susceptible, and often
﻿exhibit rapid symptom development post-transmission.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:03.970
﻿As she said.

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:07.680
﻿What would you do, having a child's body and all, Conan-kun?

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:08.470
﻿Shut up.

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:11.810
﻿Regardless, Hattori...

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:12.730
﻿It's been bugging me...

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:16.810
﻿About why the assailant group destroyed the lab, right?

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:22.030
﻿﻿If their aim was merely to steal the bacteria, they
﻿would have no reason for blowing up the place.

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:23.150
﻿That's true.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:27.620
﻿At any rate, you know anything about
﻿this "Red Siamese Cats" organization?

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:33.500
﻿No, I only know they targeted financial
﻿groups through terrorism ten-plus years ago.

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:36.710
﻿Well, we were both kids at that time.

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:39.040
﻿Oh, my apologies.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:41.010
﻿You're still a kid now, huh?

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:42.550
﻿That's enough.

00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:45.720
﻿By the way, Kudou...

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:47.930
﻿You said you're going to be on that airship, right?

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:50.970
The one that's flying from Tokyo to here in Osaka.

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:51.810
Yeah.

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:57.600
﻿That old man that never learns his lesson
﻿issued another challenge notice to Kid.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:01.780
﻿And that guy also relayed his confirmation a little while ago.

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:05.860
﻿﻿Right now, I bet that old man's...

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:09.660
﻿You damned bunch of red stray cats!

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:15.910
﻿You just robbed me of my front page news about the
﻿largest airship in the world being under my command!

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:22.760
﻿Thanks to you, even my challenge notice to my nemesis
﻿Kaitou Kid has been buried within the back pages!

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:25.760
﻿﻿In that case, Kudou...

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:29.090
﻿Stay at my place after you arrive.

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:32.100
﻿I'll take you to that okonomiyaki restaurant I promised.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:34.310
﻿Yeah, got it.

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:34.810
﻿Later.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:00.460
﻿﻿I'm high school detective, Kudou Shinichi.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:04.250
﻿While visiting an amusement park with my 
childhood friend and classmate, Mouri Ran...

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:08.090
﻿I witnessed a man in black in the midst of a suspicious transaction.

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:10.720
﻿﻿While caught up in watching the deal...

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:13.310
﻿﻿I failed to notice his partner coming up behind me.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.730
﻿﻿Those men forced me to swallow poison...

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:20.940
﻿﻿And when I came to...

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:23.190
﻿﻿My body had shrunk.

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:26.780
﻿﻿If those guys found out that Kudou Shinichi was still alive...

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:28.320
﻿﻿They'd come after me again...

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:30.200
﻿﻿And put those around me at risk.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:33.370
﻿﻿At Professor Agasa's suggestion, I decided to conceal my true identity.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:35.330
﻿﻿When Ran asked for my name, in that instant...

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:37.040
﻿﻿I became Edogawa Conan.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:39.370
﻿﻿In order to obtain information on those guys...

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:42.330
﻿﻿I went to live with Ran, whose father is a private detective.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:53.550
Suzuki Jirokichi, 72 years old.

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:54.810
﻿Excuse me!

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:00.060
Thank you very much.

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:02.520
He's the cousin of the dad of Suzuki Sonoko, Ran's best friend...

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:04.610
And is an advisor to the Suzuki Financial Group.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:07.230
﻿﻿This old man obtained all the trophies he yearned for...

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:10.240
﻿﻿And bragged about having fulfilled all his dreams.

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:15.410
﻿﻿Now, he's obsessed with battling Kid.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.370
﻿﻿But...

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:20.040
﻿﻿What has my attention now is them...

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:25.460
The terrorists that decimated the research
facility and stole the dangerous bacteria.

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:28.550
﻿﻿What exactly is their aim?

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:32.930
﻿﻿Even though I've become smaller, my mind remains the same...

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:35.140
﻿﻿The unbeaten great detective...

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:37.220
﻿﻿There's always only one truth!

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:47.520
﻿It's Tropical Land!

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:50.070
﻿The castle looks so small!

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:51.740
﻿Just like an amusement park model!

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:55.160
﻿What a sight, what a sight!

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:58.120
﻿Dad, the view's really great!

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:01.250
﻿Hey, why not come take a look?

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:02.370
﻿Shut up!

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:03.870
﻿I've got a lot on my mind right now!

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:05.540
Geez...

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:09.210
﻿Come to think of it, Mouri-kun is afraid of heights, isn't he?

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:10.130
﻿It's not like that!

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:16.090
﻿Say, do you think Kid-san always enjoys scenery like this?

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:17.890
﻿How I envy him!

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:19.310
﻿But still...

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:21.180
﻿Are you sure Kid will actually come?

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:22.520
﻿Of course he will.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:26.060
﻿He even sent a reply to Uncle Jirokichi.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:31.490
﻿Henogo... ndeo... keshimasu?

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:37.370
﻿Hey, you—it won't make sense if you only read the hiragana!

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:39.830
﻿Geez.

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:41.080
﻿Listen!

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:45.580
﻿"I cordially accept your invitation to board your airship.

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:52.460
﻿However, I simply could not bear witnessing a 72-year-old
﻿senior in such a nervous state over a six hour flight.

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:57.550
﻿Instead, I will only take possession of the gem
﻿once the airship begins to near Osaka City.

00:08:57.550 --> 00:09:01.270
﻿Please do enjoy your flight until then.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:02.720
﻿Kaitou Kid.

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:07.730
﻿I wonder if he would come take me into his possession too?

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:09.400
﻿Kid-sama!

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.530
﻿I've been considering this for some time, but...

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:13.780
﻿She really does have a unique personality.

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:15.070
﻿Could say that.

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:18.950
﻿Speaking of which, are we the only passengers on board?

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:23.540
﻿I recall a reportage writer named Fujioka-san...

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:25.160
﻿That guy!

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:29.420
﻿Fujioka Takamichi

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:29.420
﻿Reportage Writer

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:29.040
He insisted we allow him to write a report on
the battle between Kid and Uncle Jirokichi...

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:31.590
﻿And offered us his services.

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:32.710
﻿Other than him...

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:34.050
﻿Hello, excuse me!

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:36.880
﻿Would you happen to be Mouri Kogorou-san?

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:38.930
Nice to meet you.

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:42.510
﻿Mizukawa Masaki

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:42.510
﻿Nichiuri TV Director

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:45.060
﻿And also...

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:47.980
I also have one of our reporters, Nishitani Kasumi...

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:51.820
﻿Ishimoto Junpei

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:51.820
﻿Cameraman

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:51.820
﻿Nishitani Kasumi

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:51.820
﻿Reporter

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:50.190
And our cameraman, Ishimoto Junpei.

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:52.070
Pleased to meet you.

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:53.780
﻿Likewise.

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:59.200
﻿This time, with regards to the battle between Mr. Suzuki
﻿and Kid, our station will be offering an exclusive broadcast.

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:02.370
﻿If I'm not mistaken, isn't it supposed
﻿to be a special program this evening?

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:02.870
﻿Yes!

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:09.460
﻿To be honest, we wish we could do a headline presentation
﻿just like when he performed his miraculous mid-air walk, but...

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:11.290
﻿Now is a bad time.

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:12.380
﻿Bad time?

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:15.010
﻿You mean the Red Siamese Cats.

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:16.420
﻿Yeah.

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:20.180
Ever since their manifesto proclaimed they'd
﻿make their next move within seven days...

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:22.640
﻿Our entire station has been on high alert!

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:26.520
﻿﻿If the manifesto proclamation was
﻿genuine, today is the final day.

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:32.610
Thanks to them, I couldn't get a flight permit for the
﻿helicopter I prepared for my autobiographical movie.

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:36.440
﻿What a bunch of pesky stray cats.

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:37.150
﻿Right, Lupin?

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:40.410
﻿Uncle Jirokichi!

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:43.530
﻿Greetings, Advisor Suzuki, greetings!

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:46.120
﻿I'm looking forward to working with you today.

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:49.040
A﻿t any rate, what a marvelous airship this is!

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:53.380
﻿To think you're broadcasting from such a marvelous airship...

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:55.170
﻿With a mere staff of three.

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:58.050
﻿I'm sorry.

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:00.880
﻿That incident has all the hands at our station tied.

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:05.890
﻿Come to think of it, what are the
﻿culprits going to do with the bacteria?

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:06.850
﻿Yeah, yeah.

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:09.430
﻿They say you can't be saved once you're infected, right?

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:12.980
I heard it spreads by droplet contact (himatsu kansen).

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:14.520
﻿That's so scary!

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:16.730
So they'll spread it with cold soup noodles (hiyashi tanmen)?

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:18.240
﻿It's by droplet contact (himatsu kansen).

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:20.070
﻿It means it spreads by coughing or sneezing.

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:24.070
﻿They say children are most easily infected, so look out for yourselves.

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:26.910
﻿Don't fret.

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:30.660
﻿I don't care if it's killer bacteria or something else.

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:34.920
﻿I've flown to many places where germs move about like crazy...

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:36.630
﻿And I'm still as healthy as a horse.

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:40.050
﻿We human beings are stronger than germs.

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:40.800
﻿That's right!

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:42.340
﻿Then again...

00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:45.640
﻿If it's you little brats, you might just croak and be gone!

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:48.600
﻿Please stop.

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:51.270
﻿Don't say things that will frighten the children.

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:53.350
﻿That's right, you're too inconsiderate!

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:56.400
﻿No harm done!

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:57.480
﻿Don't worry.

00:11:57.480 --> 00:12:00.990
﻿Even if the bacteria is being spread elsewhere in Japan...

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:03.700
﻿As long as we're in this airship, we'll be fine.

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:04.700
﻿Rest assured!

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:09.290
﻿That is, if this thing flies forever.

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:18.420
﻿Huh?

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:20.210
﻿Isn't it almost time to prepare the tea?

00:12:21.380 --> 00:12:23.180
﻿But before that I'd like to take a puff.

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:24.930
﻿I'll be back soon.

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:56.210
﻿You're still unable to identify the culprits?

00:12:57.580 --> 00:13:02.170
Even the former executives of the Red Siamese Cats
﻿now serving sentences insisted they knew nothing.

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:06.720
﻿Our only lead at the moment is that ampule, but...

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:09.850
﻿It didn't originate from any known
﻿manufacturer inside or outside the country

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:13.680
﻿Most likely, it's safe to assume this is a Red Siamese Cats original.

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:18.230
﻿This ampule being dropped in the parking
﻿lot of the research facility suggests...

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:24.820
﻿It's highly probable the culprits brought
﻿with them a number of empty ampules.

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:31.620
﻿And they might've transfered the bacteria housed inside
﻿the facility into the ampules and transported them out.

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:36.710
﻿Then, it seems likely they dropped one of the empty ampules by mistake.

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:37.330
﻿Yeah.

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:42.750
﻿Transferring the bacteria to another vessel is
﻿an exceedingly difficult and hazardous task.

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:47.510
﻿We can assume that the culprits possess
﻿a high degree of scientific intelligence.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:52.350
﻿But, why didn't they just take them away as-is
﻿instead of risking that dangerous transfer?

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:57.640
﻿In fact, why did they resurface like ghosts after ten years of silence?

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:01.610
﻿What is it they're after?

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:10.320
﻿There are windows over here too!

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:13.950
﻿Those kids are really enjoying themselves.

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:14.370
﻿Yeah.

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:18.290
﻿To think they're able to ride an airship at such a young age...

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:20.670
﻿We really need to thank Sonoko-kun for this.

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:22.920
﻿To those kids...

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:27.050
﻿It must be like riding a piece of a floating cloud in the big sky.

00:14:29.590 --> 00:14:30.930
﻿It's nothing.

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:33.100
﻿I just remembered something from my childhood.

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:38.520
﻿When Ran first saw a flying airship, she said...

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:40.730
﻿Shinichi, this is big, real big!

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:42.190
﻿﻿There's an UFO!

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:43.150
﻿﻿An UFO is flying around!

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:44.730
﻿﻿UFO?

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:50.160
﻿Well, a balloon resembling a monster was flying leisurely in the sky.

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:51.950
﻿I suppose she must've been really surprised as she said that.

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:57.450
﻿What, bragging about your fairytale princess’s anecdotes?

00:14:58.250 --> 00:14:59.500
﻿I'm not bragging...

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:03.460
﻿But, she was already such an appealing girl back then.

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:08.920
﻿Even I long to ride this magic ship flying in the sky...

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:12.430
﻿And fly atop the clouds on my way to Dreamland.

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:17.310
﻿I'm joking.

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:18.770
﻿Of course.

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:20.440
﻿Everyone!

00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:24.650
﻿Uncle Jirokichi said he's taking us on a tour of the sky deck.

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:26.360
﻿We can see the big jewel!

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:28.110
﻿All right!

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:30.070
﻿Treasure, treasure!

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:34.450
﻿All right, you guys wanna see the treasure?

00:15:34.450 --> 00:15:35.580
﻿Yeah!

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:36.370
﻿Then, let's go!

00:15:36.740 --> 00:15:37.950
﻿Yeah!

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:40.040
﻿You guys come too, Conan-kun

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:46.670
﻿Well, in order to prevent her from being taken away
﻿by some Peter Pan and flying to Dreamland...

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:48.960
﻿Be sure to keep a tight rein.

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:51.010
﻿What's that supposed to mean?

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:52.680
﻿Professor...

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:56.430
﻿About the UFO story earlier, keep it a secret from Ran.

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:57.760
﻿I know.

00:16:06.310 --> 00:16:08.150
﻿Is everybody here?

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:08.980
﻿Yeah!

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:16.070
In that case, allow me, Chief Steward Asano, to treat you to a tour of the sky deck.

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:15.490
﻿Asano Mitsuhiro

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:15.490
﻿Chief Steward

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:19.700
﻿Awesome!

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:22.500
﻿Look, there are glass windows everywhere!

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:25.210
﻿We can see the interior of the airship!

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:26.540
﻿Well then, let us take off.

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:28.960
Everyone, prepare for a surprise.

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:28.170
﻿How exciting, right?

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:37.390
﻿About this Bell Tree 1st...

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:39.890
﻿The total length is 246 meters.

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:42.520
﻿The longest measure of diameter is 42.2 meters.

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:45.350
﻿Compared to the famous Hindenburg...

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:49.070
﻿It's longer by one meter in both length and diameter.

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:51.820
﻿It is indeed the world's largest airship.

00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:53.530
﻿Damn...

00:16:53.530 --> 00:16:56.240
﻿Why is this place surrounded by glass?

00:16:56.240 --> 00:17:01.830
﻿In the cockpit, we have the latest computerized
﻿control system installed and at our disposal.

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:06.500
﻿Hey, there are things that look like balloons floating up there!

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:10.170
﻿Those are called "ballonets" and are filled with helium gas.

00:17:10.210 --> 00:17:12.380
﻿They look just like a whale's lungs.

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:13.420
﻿It's true!

00:17:13.420 --> 00:17:14.670
﻿They look so alive!

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:18.680
﻿It really feels like we're ascending into the belly of a whale.

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:26.520
﻿How bright!

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:29.400
﻿We can see the sky!

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:34.030
﻿Treasure!

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:40.620
﻿This is the place that Advisor Suzuki is so proud of...

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:41.790
﻿The sky deck!

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:44.910
﻿Part of the roof can be opened and closed.

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:47.040
﻿It's good for sunbathing...

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:48.960
﻿And is more than suitable for stargazing.

00:17:49.210 --> 00:17:51.380
﻿Though there are many ways to have fun...

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:57.010
﻿This time, in order to capture that guy, I added a little something.

00:17:57.260 --> 00:17:58.970
﻿Show me the treasure!

00:17:58.970 --> 00:18:00.470
﻿It's not something you kids need to see!

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:02.970
﻿Shouldn't it be all right?

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:03.640
﻿No!

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:06.180
Hey, you!

00:18:08.230 --> 00:18:09.600
﻿You...

00:18:09.600 --> 00:18:11.060
﻿Inspector Nakamori!

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:12.150
﻿Oh, Mouri-san.

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:12.820
﻿You're here too.

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:14.070
﻿Allow me to show you.

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:15.190
﻿Wait up!

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:19.450
﻿That's the lapis lazuli I'm using as bait on that guy.

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:21.700
﻿The big jewel, Lady Sky.

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:23.120
﻿Beautiful!

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:26.700
﻿This blue color possesses a certain je ne sais quoi.

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:29.460
﻿The golden grains are sparkling!

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:31.170
﻿Just like the stars!

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:34.960
﻿Look at the largest spot among the golden grains.

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:36.840
﻿Doesn't it look like something?

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:41.430
﻿The largest spot, you mean?

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:46.020
﻿It looks just like a woman's face!

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:48.020
﻿That's correct.

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:50.900
﻿That is the reasoning behind the name "Lady Sky".

00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:58.820
﻿Even the ancient Roman natural historian Mulanius
described it as, "A fragment of the starry firmament".

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:03.660
﻿It certainly is most suitable for it to be displayed on this sky deck.

00:19:04.740 --> 00:19:10.540
So why are you displaying such an invaluable
 ﻿treasure in a plain, ordinary glass case?

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:16.590
﻿The glass is bulletproof, able to deflect
﻿bullets even from machine guns...

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:22.010
﻿And won't open without both the input of
﻿my fingerprint and a certain passcode.

00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:24.300
﻿Don't you realize this system is as strong as steel?

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:27.810
﻿Something like that won't help us at all.

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:32.850
In fact, the research facility where the bacteria
was stolen from utilized a similar setup.

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:32.400
﻿What'll happen if we press this?

00:19:32.980 --> 00:19:34.520
﻿Why don't you press it and find out?

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:38.190
﻿Just like this, what will happen?

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:40.030
﻿Hey!

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:51.290
﻿They didn't have a trap like this in their system, did they?

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:57.380
﻿What the hell were you doing, you stinky brat!

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:01.970
﻿Dad...

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:06.760
﻿﻿I see, there's a sensor.

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:09.600
﻿And you fall into traps too easily.

00:20:09.930 --> 00:20:11.020
﻿It's true...

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:14.310
﻿That they didn't have these traps, but...

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:16.560
﻿What would you do if he did this?

00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:24.410
﻿If he points a gun at you like this, you'll have no
﻿choice but to open it with your finger, right?

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:27.870
﻿Well, I don't imagine he'd do something like that...

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:29.080
﻿But in that case...

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:35.670
﻿Inspector Nakamori!

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:39.340
﻿In that case, I simply have to do this.

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:42.420
﻿Could it be that he's fallen into the sea?

00:20:42.420 --> 00:20:43.510
﻿Something like that won't happen.

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:48.260
﻿Damn, what the hell kind of a trap is this!?

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:50.600
﻿Do you still think it's an ordinary glass case?

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:52.390
﻿﻿If I recall, it was...

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:04.490
﻿﻿I see, so that's how it is.

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:08.370
﻿At any rate, that guy isn't going to appear until dusk.

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:11.080
﻿There's no need for you to monitor here until then, right?

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:14.410
﻿This is my operation, don't go bossing me around!

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:15.040
﻿Let's go!

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:15.670
﻿Roger!

00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:23.170
﻿My, what you've demonstrated was of great interest.

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:25.260
﻿Thanks to that, I might just cook up the perfect report.

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:27.470
﻿I'm truly sorry, but...

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:31.220
﻿Please go to the smoking room on B-deck if you wish to smoke.

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:35.140
﻿Mouri-san, how about joining me?

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:38.190
﻿Nah, I think I'm gonna head back to my room for some rest.

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:39.650
﻿I can't even tell left from right.

00:21:41.230 --> 00:21:42.530
﻿That's no wonder.

00:21:49.530 --> 00:21:50.830
﻿What a relief.

00:21:51.740 --> 00:21:53.330
﻿Uncle was really in bad shape, huh?

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:57.870
﻿By the way, those bandages were nicely done, right?

00:21:58.460 --> 00:22:00.340
﻿The bandages, the adhesive bandages.

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:02.880
﻿You didn't take a look?

00:22:04.300 --> 00:22:07.300
﻿Don't tell me, you did something to them?

00:22:08.930 --> 00:22:10.470
﻿Hey, what's this supposed to be?

00:22:14.770 --> 00:22:15.980
﻿Like it?

00:22:15.980 --> 00:22:18.190
﻿Geez, what are you doing?

00:22:19.060 --> 00:22:20.230
﻿This isn't good!

00:22:20.270 --> 00:22:23.610
﻿While I was boarding the plane, I gave some
﻿of these to one of the maintenance staff!

00:22:25.320 --> 00:22:26.990
﻿﻿Everybody, hurry!

00:22:28.150 --> 00:22:28.910
﻿﻿Got you!

00:22:31.200 --> 00:22:34.330
﻿﻿It's dangerous to run around here, little miss.

00:22:34.330 --> 00:22:35.330
﻿﻿Thank you.

00:22:35.330 --> 00:22:36.580
﻿﻿Thank you very much.

00:22:37.000 --> 00:22:37.540
﻿﻿No problem.

00:22:39.170 --> 00:22:40.080
﻿﻿It's bleeding.

00:22:40.580 --> 00:22:41.710
﻿﻿Your elbow.

00:22:43.840 --> 00:22:44.880
﻿﻿I think I skinned it.

00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:46.510
﻿﻿Hang on a second.

00:22:48.720 --> 00:22:50.220
﻿﻿Here, please apply these.

00:22:52.260 --> 00:22:52.930
﻿﻿Thank you.

00:22:55.220 --> 00:22:56.560
﻿What do I do?

00:22:56.560 --> 00:22:58.520
﻿If he thinks I did this...

00:22:58.520 --> 00:23:00.140
﻿He won't notice!

00:23:00.140 --> 00:23:01.810
﻿The writing's small, anyway.

00:23:01.810 --> 00:23:02.650
﻿Geez.

00:23:04.770 --> 00:23:08.780
﻿I think I'd like to go see the gem again.

00:23:09.990 --> 00:23:12.820
﻿With so many people crowding around, I couldn't get a good look.

00:23:12.820 --> 00:23:13.200
﻿Oh?

00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:15.790
﻿Then, I'm gonna get back to my room.

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:18.790
﻿I've already agreed to send some messages to Makoto-san.

00:23:18.790 --> 00:23:21.040
﻿Although I didn't tell him about Kid-sama.

00:23:21.080 --> 00:23:22.130
﻿Well, seeya for now.

00:23:34.140 --> 00:23:35.100
﻿﻿Who could that be?

00:23:40.270 --> 00:23:40.810
﻿Hello.

00:23:43.560 --> 00:23:44.520
﻿Hello.

00:23:46.110 --> 00:23:47.940
﻿I'm working as a waiter for this airship.

00:23:49.740 --> 00:23:53.950
﻿I took a little break from work to come see
 ﻿this big jewel everyone is so excited about.

00:23:55.410 --> 00:23:55.910
﻿Uh oh...

00:23:56.370 --> 00:23:57.580
﻿This is bad.

00:23:57.580 --> 00:23:58.490
﻿I really should get going.

00:23:59.830 --> 00:24:01.040
﻿Well, please enjoy yourself.

00:24:02.210 --> 00:24:02.710
﻿Yes.

00:24:07.300 --> 00:24:08.090
﻿Hold on a second!

00:24:09.800 --> 00:24:10.510
﻿What is it?

00:24:11.050 --> 00:24:12.260
﻿This bandage...

00:24:13.800 --> 00:24:15.600
﻿I burned myself a little...

00:24:15.600 --> 00:24:16.430
﻿Liar.

00:24:16.800 --> 00:24:17.760
﻿It's not a lie...

00:24:18.140 --> 00:24:20.060
﻿Then, why don't you take a good look?

00:24:20.060 --> 00:24:21.390
﻿At this bandage.

00:24:25.060 --> 00:24:25.730
﻿Not good!

00:24:26.190 --> 00:24:29.730
﻿How could you possibly have a bandage I gave to someone else?

00:24:31.070 --> 00:24:31.780
﻿You're Kid, aren't you?

00:24:32.860 --> 00:24:33.400
﻿She's got me.

00:24:34.610 --> 00:24:35.450
﻿Tell me the truth!

00:24:36.410 --> 00:24:37.990
﻿I'm screwed...

00:24:37.990 --> 00:24:39.950
﻿﻿I can't just insist I'm the waiter...

00:24:40.290 --> 00:24:42.080
﻿﻿And if I force my way out...

00:24:47.630 --> 00:24:49.170
What's so funny?

00:24:49.210 --> 00:24:50.510
﻿Hurry up and confess!

00:24:50.510 --> 00:24:52.470
﻿What will you do if I confess?

00:24:53.010 --> 00:24:56.140
﻿Are you going to keep holding onto me
﻿and deliver me to Inspector Nakamori?

00:24:57.850 --> 00:24:59.810
﻿That sounds like an interesting plan.

00:24:59.810 --> 00:25:02.350
﻿But, you'll be troubled by it if you do that.

00:25:04.980 --> 00:25:07.060
﻿Can't you tell yet?

00:25:07.060 --> 00:25:08.110
﻿Who I...

00:25:08.770 --> 00:25:09.820
﻿Really am?

00:25:12.320 --> 00:25:13.650
﻿Right.

00:25:13.650 --> 00:25:15.530
﻿The true identity of Kaitou Kid...

00:25:16.570 --> 00:25:17.620
﻿Is me.

00:25:21.290 --> 00:25:22.950
﻿Are you all right, Conan-kun?

00:25:22.950 --> 00:25:23.540
﻿Caught a cold again?

00:25:23.540 --> 00:25:24.660
﻿No, it's not a cold.

00:25:25.160 --> 00:25:26.670
﻿What's wrong?

00:25:26.670 --> 00:25:29.040
﻿Have you forgotten my face since it's been so long?

00:25:31.590 --> 00:25:34.170
﻿Shinichi is Kid's true identity?

00:25:34.170 --> 00:25:35.550
﻿Don’t make me laugh.

00:25:35.590 --> 00:25:37.010
﻿You're just playing with your disguising skills...

00:25:39.640 --> 00:25:40.140
﻿It's not?

00:25:40.600 --> 00:25:41.850
﻿Of course not!

00:25:41.850 --> 00:25:42.720
﻿This is my real face.

00:25:44.310 --> 00:25:48.350
﻿No, last time "Shinichi" also made me forcefully land a plane.

00:25:48.350 --> 00:25:51.070
The inspector pinched his face, but the mask didn't come off either.

00:25:51.610 --> 00:25:53.360
﻿You just happen to have a face similar to his, no?

00:25:55.490 --> 00:25:57.780
﻿Damn, I was being careless!

00:25:58.610 --> 00:26:00.910
﻿That guy will definitely come check the surroundings before his crime!

00:26:01.450 --> 00:26:02.740
If we leave the jewel alone...

00:26:01.950 --> 00:26:03.080
﻿Inspector Nakamori!

00:26:07.750 --> 00:26:10.960
﻿You're just unlucky for riding on an airship
 ﻿where your escape routes are cut off.

00:26:11.630 --> 00:26:13.050
﻿Face the consequences!

00:26:23.760 --> 00:26:25.180
﻿It's not an airship.

00:26:25.980 --> 00:26:26.980
﻿It's an UFO.

00:26:30.900 --> 00:26:33.860
﻿I remember you saying something like that when you were little.

00:26:34.570 --> 00:26:42.070
﻿I presume that even now you see me as an unidentifiable
 ﻿alien who just jumped out of an UFO all of a sudden, but...

00:26:42.070 --> 00:26:45.580
﻿I dress up as Kaitou Kid in order to
 ﻿solve cases, not because I want to.

00:26:47.000 --> 00:26:51.250
﻿As proof, I always return the jewels back to their owners, right?

00:26:52.840 --> 00:26:53.590
﻿But...

00:26:54.130 --> 00:26:54.840
﻿Then...

00:26:56.170 --> 00:27:02.300
Well, as the great detective Kudou Shinichi, I
 ﻿can't just let that grandiose thief run amok.

00:27:02.300 --> 00:27:04.390
﻿And I thought you would understand, but...

00:27:05.430 --> 00:27:07.180
﻿Since I'm in your hands, I can only comply.

00:27:07.930 --> 00:27:08.890
﻿I'll surrender.

00:27:09.940 --> 00:27:11.690
﻿Shinichi...

00:27:12.690 --> 00:27:13.400
﻿What's wrong?

00:27:14.400 --> 00:27:15.610
﻿There a problem?

00:27:16.440 --> 00:27:17.280
﻿No...

00:27:20.570 --> 00:27:22.910
﻿If you noticed something...

00:27:22.910 --> 00:27:24.370
﻿Oh, it's nothing!

00:27:24.660 --> 00:27:26.490
﻿I just misunderstood something!

00:27:26.490 --> 00:27:27.580
﻿My apologies.

00:27:27.580 --> 00:27:28.290
﻿Bye!

00:27:33.130 --> 00:27:34.130
﻿What does this mean?

00:27:34.590 --> 00:27:36.380
﻿Does that mean Shinichi really is Kid?

00:27:37.170 --> 00:27:41.590
﻿When he told me he was busy solving cases
﻿was he actually going around stealing things?

00:27:48.270 --> 00:27:50.690
﻿Hey, could you get those glasses over there for me?

00:27:52.940 --> 00:27:54.190
﻿What's wrong with your arm?

00:27:55.730 --> 00:27:58.570
﻿It just feels like a mosquito bit me—it's really itchy.

00:27:58.570 --> 00:28:01.200
﻿Geez, who'd have thought we'd have mosquitoes in a place like this.

00:28:01.530 --> 00:28:01.900
﻿Here.

00:28:01.900 --> 00:28:02.740
﻿Thank you.

00:28:11.620 --> 00:28:12.040
﻿Well then.

00:28:22.970 --> 00:28:24.090
﻿I...

00:28:24.090 --> 00:28:25.340
﻿Still don't believe you.

00:28:25.340 --> 00:28:26.930
﻿Then, if you'll excuse me.

00:28:40.530 --> 00:28:41.740
﻿Time!

00:28:42.700 --> 00:28:43.740
Fujioka-san!

00:28:44.950 --> 00:28:46.320
﻿My bad, my bad.

00:28:46.320 --> 00:28:49.580
﻿As expected from a Kantou karate champion.

00:28:49.580 --> 00:28:50.750
﻿You have such nice muscles!

00:29:27.200 --> 00:29:28.450
﻿Hey, look!

00:29:28.450 --> 00:29:29.370
﻿An airship!

00:29:29.990 --> 00:29:31.330
﻿Awesome!

00:29:31.330 --> 00:29:32.330
﻿Just like a whale!

00:29:32.790 --> 00:29:34.540
﻿A whale flying in the sky!

00:29:37.540 --> 00:29:38.460
﻿Sorry for the wait.

00:29:43.880 --> 00:29:45.470
﻿Fabulous!

00:29:45.470 --> 00:29:47.090
﻿Miss, one more glass!

00:29:49.890 --> 00:29:51.560
﻿Looks like Uncle's back to his old self.

00:29:51.970 --> 00:29:53.680
﻿And what's with the "miss"?

00:29:55.230 --> 00:29:56.940
﻿Apologies for the wait.

00:29:56.940 --> 00:29:58.440
﻿Your dessert cake is here.

00:29:59.190 --> 00:29:59.810
﻿Thanks...

00:30:05.070 --> 00:30:06.740
﻿I've been waiting for it.

00:30:06.740 --> 00:30:07.740
﻿Looks delicious!

00:30:08.110 --> 00:30:08.990
﻿Huh?

00:30:09.030 --> 00:30:11.780
﻿What's this inside the cream?

00:30:13.540 --> 00:30:15.750
﻿It looks like a blackberry!

00:30:16.660 --> 00:30:17.250
﻿Hey, Ran.

00:30:18.580 --> 00:30:19.580
﻿Ran, hello!

00:30:20.420 --> 00:30:22.920
﻿Why are you staring at him with a serious face?

00:30:24.000 --> 00:30:26.760
﻿You trying to tell me he's your type?

00:30:26.800 --> 00:30:28.220
﻿That's not it at all...

00:30:28.220 --> 00:30:30.430
﻿I'm gonna report this to your hubby!

00:30:30.430 --> 00:30:32.010
﻿I said that's not it!

00:30:37.850 --> 00:30:38.890
﻿As I said...

00:30:39.140 --> 00:30:42.570
﻿If we open this door, we can get out from this middle passage.

00:30:43.150 --> 00:30:45.230
﻿And if we get out from the door ahead of it...

00:30:45.230 --> 00:30:46.740
﻿We'll be there.

00:30:46.740 --> 00:30:47.530
﻿That's right.

00:30:48.990 --> 00:30:49.490
You guys...

00:30:50.200 --> 00:30:51.370
﻿Are you going somewhere?

00:30:52.120 --> 00:30:53.620
﻿No, we're...

00:30:53.620 --> 00:30:57.040
﻿Just planning to play cards in our room after this!

00:30:59.920 --> 00:31:02.290
﻿﻿I see they're up to no good again.

00:31:03.130 --> 00:31:04.590
﻿I can't wait!

00:31:05.130 --> 00:31:08.550
﻿I hope we can get to Osaka quickly and meet Kid-sama!

00:31:09.470 --> 00:31:10.970
﻿And I do hope...

00:31:11.890 --> 00:31:16.140
﻿That I can pucker up my lips against his arrogant ones...

00:31:16.470 --> 00:31:17.430
﻿No, no!

00:31:17.430 --> 00:31:18.930
﻿You absolutely cannot do that!

00:31:23.310 --> 00:31:25.150
﻿Kid is a criminal, right?

00:31:25.150 --> 00:31:26.360
﻿That's just imprudent!

00:31:27.110 --> 00:31:28.780
﻿Why are you so worked up?

00:31:29.450 --> 00:31:30.110
﻿No reason.

00:31:33.200 --> 00:31:34.410
﻿What now?

00:31:34.410 --> 00:31:35.080
﻿Nothing.

00:31:35.740 --> 00:31:37.830
﻿You guys, hurry it up!

00:31:37.830 --> 00:31:38.660
﻿Roger!

00:31:39.540 --> 00:31:43.380
﻿Inspector Nakamori, why don't you take it easy?

00:31:43.380 --> 00:31:46.340
﻿I'll have my subordinates watch the treasure.

00:31:46.340 --> 00:31:48.510
﻿But while we're taking it easy, Kid could be...

00:31:48.510 --> 00:31:49.970
﻿Thanks for the meal!

00:31:50.550 --> 00:31:53.720
﻿Then, we'll be playing cards in our room!

00:31:53.720 --> 00:31:54.430
﻿Excuse us!

00:31:55.430 --> 00:31:56.850
﻿Why are you in such a hurry?

00:31:57.260 --> 00:31:57.970
﻿Thank you.

00:32:01.100 --> 00:32:01.730
﻿Sorry.

00:32:02.230 --> 00:32:02.980
﻿Geez...

00:32:02.980 --> 00:32:04.810
﻿Be more careful, will you?

00:32:04.810 --> 00:32:10.440
﻿When you're about to sneeze, didn't your
﻿mom tell you to cover your mouth like this?

00:32:10.440 --> 00:32:11.240
﻿I'm sorry.

00:32:11.530 --> 00:32:12.400
﻿It's all right.

00:32:12.700 --> 00:32:13.660
﻿Let's go!

00:32:19.080 --> 00:32:20.330
﻿Who could this be?

00:32:21.710 --> 00:32:22.540
﻿Hello?

00:32:23.170 --> 00:32:26.920
﻿﻿We've released the killer bacteria in the airship's smoking room.

00:32:26.920 --> 00:32:27.340
﻿What?

00:32:28.590 --> 00:32:30.550
﻿What the hell is this nonsense?

00:32:30.550 --> 00:32:32.470
﻿﻿Look under the sofa on the left side of the room.

00:32:33.260 --> 00:32:34.180
﻿Hey, wait!

00:32:36.180 --> 00:32:38.060
﻿Is something wrong, Uncle?

00:32:38.850 --> 00:32:40.470
﻿Oh, not a thing.

00:32:40.470 --> 00:32:42.640
﻿Just someone making a prank call.

00:33:04.870 --> 00:33:05.620
﻿Inspector...

00:33:08.630 --> 00:33:09.630
﻿This is...

00:33:12.920 --> 00:33:14.050
﻿There's no mistake about it.

00:33:15.130 --> 00:33:19.050
﻿It's the same as the ampule left by the
 ﻿group that targeted the research facility.

00:33:19.050 --> 00:33:22.020
﻿The information regarding the ampule has not been leaked

00:33:22.020 --> 00:33:22.810
﻿﻿Which means...

00:33:23.770 --> 00:33:26.480
﻿The man who made the call was probably telling the truth.

00:33:27.190 --> 00:33:31.820
﻿It's possible the first ampule was purposely
﻿left behind in the parking lot by them...

00:33:31.820 --> 00:33:35.490
﻿In order to validate a comparison against
﻿the one now left in the smoking room.

00:33:35.820 --> 00:33:36.950
Damn!

00:33:36.950 --> 00:33:39.830
﻿﻿At any rate, I'll report this to the higher-ups.

00:33:40.280 --> 00:33:41.330
﻿Thanks.

00:33:42.290 --> 00:33:44.080
﻿It appears that man was telling the truth.

00:33:44.750 --> 00:33:45.750
﻿That's unbelievable!

00:33:46.500 --> 00:33:48.960
﻿Now is no longer the time to catch Kid.

00:33:49.750 --> 00:33:51.420
﻿Seal off the smoking room immediately!

00:33:52.090 --> 00:33:55.470
﻿To be safe, it's best we seal off this bar as well.

00:34:01.100 --> 00:34:02.260
No way!

00:34:02.260 --> 00:34:03.850
﻿Are you certain?

00:34:03.850 --> 00:34:04.980
﻿Could it be a joke?

00:34:05.560 --> 00:34:09.810
﻿No, unfortunately, this was confirmed true by headquarters.

00:34:12.400 --> 00:34:16.280
﻿At any rate, as I just said, we're sealing off the B-deck smoking room.

00:34:28.960 --> 00:34:29.750
﻿Help me...

00:34:31.250 --> 00:34:31.710
﻿Rashes?

00:34:32.380 --> 00:34:33.130
﻿Don't tell me...

00:34:33.130 --> 00:34:34.590
﻿That guy's infected?

00:34:34.590 --> 00:34:36.800
﻿Come to think of it, he was in the smoking room!

00:34:37.220 --> 00:34:38.880
﻿Help me!

00:34:38.880 --> 00:34:39.470
﻿I'm begging you!

00:34:40.340 --> 00:34:41.890
﻿I'm not feeling well!

00:34:43.100 --> 00:34:44.100
﻿Remain calm!

00:34:44.100 --> 00:34:45.020
﻿Please remain calm!

00:34:45.350 --> 00:34:46.810
﻿I don't want to die!

00:35:00.200 --> 00:35:00.860
﻿Thanks...

00:35:01.370 --> 00:35:02.160
﻿It's nothing.

00:35:02.160 --> 00:35:05.540
﻿Ran-kun, it's best that you disinfect your hands now.

00:35:05.540 --> 00:35:06.330
﻿Come here!

00:35:06.790 --> 00:35:09.290
﻿We have alcohol-based sanitizers in the prep room.

00:35:09.330 --> 00:35:10.000
﻿Yes!

00:35:12.130 --> 00:35:15.340
﻿To think someone's infected in this airship...

00:35:15.920 --> 00:35:17.920
﻿Who else entered the smoking room?

00:35:20.470 --> 00:35:21.760
﻿Wait, are you all right?

00:35:23.680 --> 00:35:24.260
﻿Rashes!

00:35:24.850 --> 00:35:26.470
﻿On her right hand and her left arm!

00:35:27.810 --> 00:35:28.680
﻿Damn...

00:35:28.680 --> 00:35:29.480
﻿Her too?

00:35:30.480 --> 00:35:32.600
﻿Is there a place we can quarantine the two of them?

00:35:33.150 --> 00:35:36.150
﻿We do have beds for patients in
﻿the back of the examination room.

00:35:36.190 --> 00:35:40.200
There aren't any doctors aboard, but we
 ﻿can lock them in from the outside there.

00:35:40.740 --> 00:35:42.070
﻿All right, let's do that immediately.

00:35:42.660 --> 00:35:43.820
﻿I'll show you the way.

00:35:45.120 --> 00:35:45.490
Hey!

00:35:45.990 --> 00:35:46.370
﻿Roger!

00:35:50.460 --> 00:35:53.670
﻿As an added precaution, let's seal off this dining room as well.

00:35:54.790 --> 00:35:57.880
﻿In that case, everyone move to the lounge!

00:35:59.300 --> 00:36:00.420
﻿Dad!

00:36:00.420 --> 00:36:01.260
﻿Wake up!

00:36:02.590 --> 00:36:06.430
﻿In any case, it's a relief those kids aren't here.

00:36:06.470 --> 00:36:06.890
﻿Yeah...

00:36:08.020 --> 00:36:11.310
﻿That's right, we need to inform the kids about this too.

00:36:12.020 --> 00:36:12.900
﻿You're right.

00:36:17.230 --> 00:36:17.770
﻿﻿Sorry.

00:36:18.820 --> 00:36:19.610
﻿﻿Not good!

00:36:20.780 --> 00:36:22.150
﻿That was fun!

00:36:22.150 --> 00:36:23.030
﻿Definitely!

00:36:23.990 --> 00:36:26.910
﻿Let's go visit the tail of the whale this time.

00:36:27.240 --> 00:36:27.530
﻿Genta-kun...

00:36:28.200 --> 00:36:30.500
﻿A whale doesn't have a tail.

00:36:30.500 --> 00:36:31.460
﻿It has a caudal fin.

00:36:31.460 --> 00:36:31.960
I see.

00:36:31.960 --> 00:36:32.620
Genta!

00:36:35.080 --> 00:36:36.290
Conan-kun.

00:36:36.340 --> 00:36:39.710
﻿Oh, I didn't know this was a restricted access area...

00:36:39.710 --> 00:36:40.300
﻿Genta!

00:36:41.130 --> 00:36:42.630
Are you feeling all right?

00:36:44.010 --> 00:36:45.390
﻿﻿He doesn't have any rashes yet.

00:36:45.720 --> 00:36:46.970
﻿Maybe he didn't catch it?

00:36:47.300 --> 00:36:49.560
﻿﻿Or, could it just be in a state of latency?

00:36:49.560 --> 00:36:51.020
﻿Hey, Conan?

00:36:51.520 --> 00:36:52.680
What's wrong?

00:36:52.680 --> 00:36:53.850
﻿I know!

00:36:53.850 --> 00:36:56.230
﻿Let's all go explore the inside of the airship!

00:36:56.360 --> 00:36:58.150
Now's not time for that.

00:36:58.150 --> 00:37:00.110
﻿Something terrible has happened.

00:37:00.110 --> 00:37:01.740
Something terrible?

00:37:01.940 --> 00:37:03.490
﻿At any rate, let's return to the cabin.

00:37:10.950 --> 00:37:11.620
Hide!

00:37:13.250 --> 00:37:14.250
﻿Stay put right here.

00:37:22.210 --> 00:37:23.340
﻿﻿Who is that?

00:37:23.800 --> 00:37:25.220
﻿﻿Going there at a time like this...

00:37:25.680 --> 00:37:26.680
﻿﻿What on earth...

00:37:35.230 --> 00:37:36.270
﻿The sound of a lock...

00:37:37.400 --> 00:37:39.190
﻿﻿Could it be that person has the bacteria?

00:37:41.610 --> 00:37:42.990
﻿Who is that person?

00:37:43.530 --> 00:37:45.070
﻿An accomplice of Kid's?

00:37:45.110 --> 00:37:45.700
Geez...

00:37:46.450 --> 00:37:47.070
﻿That's not it.

00:37:48.370 --> 00:37:50.620
﻿I don't think that was an accomplice of Kid.

00:37:52.120 --> 00:37:54.750
﻿More likely, they're with the Red Siamese Cats.

00:37:57.460 --> 00:37:58.210
﻿Not good...

00:37:59.540 --> 00:38:00.380
﻿This is not good!

00:38:10.760 --> 00:38:11.350
Damn!

00:38:43.460 --> 00:38:44.210
﻿﻿Those are...

00:38:45.210 --> 00:38:46.170
﻿Bombs?

00:38:50.340 --> 00:38:51.350
﻿Get to the back.

00:38:52.640 --> 00:38:54.600
﻿Climb up the ladder next to the gas shaft!

00:38:58.100 --> 00:38:58.940
﻿Hurry, hurry!

00:40:21.940 --> 00:40:22.390
﻿Don't move!

00:40:25.770 --> 00:40:27.110
﻿Who the hell are you?

00:40:29.570 --> 00:40:31.150
﻿Did you find the ampule?

00:40:32.360 --> 00:40:33.490
﻿The Red Siamese Cats...

00:40:35.070 --> 00:40:36.950
﻿I've planted bombs on this ship.

00:40:37.830 --> 00:40:41.790
﻿So long as you control yourselves and hear
﻿me out, I will refrain from detonating them.

00:40:43.620 --> 00:40:45.460
﻿Now Lupin, simmer down!

00:40:53.340 --> 00:40:55.090
﻿I told you to behave!

00:40:56.430 --> 00:40:57.140
﻿How are things going?

00:40:57.640 --> 00:40:59.760
﻿Cat-F, cockpit under control.

00:41:00.100 --> 00:41:02.100
﻿Cat-D, kitchen under control.

00:41:02.480 --> 00:41:04.730
﻿Cat-C, sky deck under control.

00:41:05.560 --> 00:41:07.150
﻿The guest rooms are vacant.

00:41:08.060 --> 00:41:08.900
﻿Good.

00:41:09.860 --> 00:41:13.070
﻿Tell the entire crew to gather in the dining room using the PA system.

00:41:16.200 --> 00:41:16.990
﻿Conan-kun...

00:41:17.660 --> 00:41:18.580
﻿What should we do?

00:41:18.990 --> 00:41:20.830
﻿﻿Attention flight attendants.

00:41:20.830 --> 00:41:23.290
﻿﻿Report to the dining room as soon as possible.

00:41:24.040 --> 00:41:25.250
﻿﻿I repeat:

00:41:25.250 --> 00:41:29.000
﻿﻿All flight attendants should report to
﻿the dining room as soon as possible.

00:41:41.350 --> 00:41:45.480
﻿We, the Red Siamese Cats, have hijacked this airship.

00:41:49.860 --> 00:41:52.440
﻿Everyone, surrender your cell phones.

00:42:00.870 --> 00:42:02.370
﻿Dad, wake up!

00:42:08.380 --> 00:42:09.460
﻿I don't have one.

00:42:17.220 --> 00:42:17.510
﻿It's me.

00:42:18.050 --> 00:42:20.050
﻿The airship's been hijacked.

00:42:20.050 --> 00:42:21.260
﻿﻿As I thought.

00:42:21.260 --> 00:42:22.140
﻿﻿What are their demands?

00:42:22.600 --> 00:42:24.020
﻿Spell out your demands.

00:42:24.020 --> 00:42:27.640
﻿Is it money, or do you want your colleague inmates to be released?

00:42:28.850 --> 00:42:32.150
﻿We hold a grudge against the Suzuki Financial Group.

00:42:32.150 --> 00:42:34.320
﻿Especially against this old man.

00:42:35.690 --> 00:42:39.570
﻿It's true that I lent a hand to the police ten years ago...

00:42:40.320 --> 00:42:42.620
﻿In order to crush your organization.

00:42:43.200 --> 00:42:45.790
﻿That's why you should make me your sole hostage.

00:42:45.790 --> 00:42:47.870
﻿Please release the others.

00:42:47.870 --> 00:42:49.370
﻿I can't consent to that.

00:42:49.870 --> 00:42:50.830
Why not!?

00:42:50.830 --> 00:42:53.130
﻿This airship will head to Osaka as planned.

00:42:54.340 --> 00:42:55.800
﻿Contact the police.

00:42:56.510 --> 00:42:59.680
﻿However, should a single wrong move be made...

00:42:59.680 --> 00:43:01.890
﻿I will obliterate this ship.

00:43:01.890 --> 00:43:02.760
﻿Relay that!

00:43:03.850 --> 00:43:04.890
﻿In addition...

00:43:05.810 --> 00:43:08.060
﻿This is that killer bacteria!

00:43:08.640 --> 00:43:11.690
﻿Don't make the mistake of assuming you can arrest us.

00:43:12.400 --> 00:43:19.030
It won't just be the smoking room—instead, the killer
 ﻿bacteria will be spread throughout the entire cabin!

00:43:20.570 --> 00:43:21.950
﻿What do we do, Conan-kun?

00:43:23.240 --> 00:43:25.330
﻿We need to rescue Ai-chan and the others!

00:43:25.330 --> 00:43:27.540
﻿Before that, we need to disarm the bombs.

00:43:28.290 --> 00:43:32.880
﻿Haibara, there may be accomplices among the hostages.

00:43:32.880 --> 00:43:33.670
﻿Be careful.

00:43:33.670 --> 00:43:34.290
﻿﻿Roger.

00:43:36.050 --> 00:43:37.050
﻿You guys...

00:43:37.050 --> 00:43:39.260
﻿Don't tell me you visited the smoking room?

00:43:40.510 --> 00:43:41.090
﻿Did you!?

00:43:42.680 --> 00:43:46.100
﻿But, we only took a little peep...

00:43:46.100 --> 00:43:50.020
﻿Because the smell of the smoke was 
so bad, I closed the door right away.

00:43:50.640 --> 00:43:51.770
﻿What the hell...

00:43:52.230 --> 00:43:54.190
﻿﻿It isn't just sneezing we have to worry
﻿about, but also the smoking room?

00:43:54.900 --> 00:43:56.150
﻿It's all right.

00:43:56.150 --> 00:43:58.360
﻿We didn't really go inside.

00:43:58.400 --> 00:44:00.070
﻿We don't have that redness either.

00:44:03.620 --> 00:44:05.620
﻿Besides that, what should we do about the bombs?

00:44:07.490 --> 00:44:09.080
﻿There are four bombs in total.

00:44:09.910 --> 00:44:15.590
﻿I suspect two of them are near the fuel tank
﻿on the back half of the passage below.

00:44:16.290 --> 00:44:16.880
﻿You guys...

00:44:19.510 --> 00:44:21.010
﻿Can you go find the bombs?

00:44:21.470 --> 00:44:22.930
﻿Of course.

00:44:22.930 --> 00:44:26.140
﻿But, don't touch them even if you do find them.

00:44:26.140 --> 00:44:27.470
﻿Contact me immediately.

00:44:28.060 --> 00:44:28.520
﻿Got it.

00:44:28.930 --> 00:44:32.480
﻿And, if you begin to feel even slightly unwell, notify me right away.

00:44:32.850 --> 00:44:33.480
﻿All right?

00:44:38.690 --> 00:44:40.990
﻿Ayumi and Mitsuhiko should be fine.

00:44:42.030 --> 00:44:43.110
﻿But Genta...

00:44:46.410 --> 00:44:47.490
﻿﻿Damn it!

00:44:47.870 --> 00:44:50.330
﻿﻿I can only hope he isn't infected.

00:44:56.080 --> 00:44:57.420
﻿Hey, what about the kids?

00:44:58.630 --> 00:45:01.010
﻿No worries, Conan-kun is with them.

00:45:17.310 --> 00:45:18.570
﻿As expected...

00:45:18.570 --> 00:45:20.320
﻿There's one right behind the smoking room.

00:45:21.190 --> 00:45:26.360
﻿If they were to detonate this, the bacteria in the
﻿smoking room would be released throughout the ship.

00:45:30.450 --> 00:45:34.250
﻿And if they were to cause a hole in the ship itself
﻿the bacteria could spread to the outside world.

00:45:37.210 --> 00:45:41.460
﻿But why did the culprits have to use both bombs and the bacteria?

00:45:42.340 --> 00:45:45.050
﻿﻿It's sufficient to just use one of them for hijacking.

00:45:49.390 --> 00:45:50.140
﻿Why?

00:45:50.760 --> 00:45:54.430
﻿Why are the culprits using both bombs and the bacteria?

00:45:55.100 --> 00:45:56.730
﻿As double insurance, perhaps?

00:45:59.150 --> 00:46:03.280
﻿In any case, unless they make a clear demand...

00:46:03.280 --> 00:46:04.900
﻿We can only wait and see.

00:46:06.950 --> 00:46:10.870
﻿Follow the airship from a distance without being discovered.

00:46:11.740 --> 00:46:16.790
﻿As for Osaka and the other prefectures in
﻿the path of the airship, I will contact them.

00:46:17.620 --> 00:46:18.580
﻿Understood.

00:46:19.670 --> 00:46:20.380
﻿﻿Conan-kun!

00:46:20.380 --> 00:46:21.670
﻿We found it—the bomb!

00:46:21.710 --> 00:46:22.960
﻿﻿And I found one too!

00:46:28.220 --> 00:46:28.970
﻿Good.

00:46:29.720 --> 00:46:30.720
﻿Only one left.

00:46:34.930 --> 00:46:35.560
﻿Get down!

00:46:46.070 --> 00:46:48.150
﻿I'll go find the last one.

00:46:48.150 --> 00:46:49.410
﻿You guys stay right here.

00:47:02.880 --> 00:47:03.920
﻿Open up.

00:47:05.670 --> 00:47:07.760
﻿Don’t try anything funny.

00:47:07.760 --> 00:47:10.680
﻿Unless you'd like to see the hostages killed.

00:47:22.860 --> 00:47:24.860
﻿What are you doing, Mizukawa-san?

00:47:25.860 --> 00:47:27.030
﻿Mizukawa-san, don't tell me...

00:47:27.780 --> 00:47:28.650
﻿It's nothing!

00:47:28.650 --> 00:47:29.490
﻿Mizukawa-san!

00:47:30.910 --> 00:47:32.660
I said it's nothing!

00:47:36.700 --> 00:47:37.540
﻿A rash!

00:47:37.580 --> 00:47:38.040
﻿No!

00:47:39.040 --> 00:47:40.370
﻿This is just hives!

00:47:40.920 --> 00:47:43.710
﻿Come to think of it, he smelled like smoke!

00:47:43.750 --> 00:47:45.500
﻿He went into the smoking room!

00:47:45.500 --> 00:47:46.460
He must've been infected...

00:47:46.460 --> 00:47:47.340
﻿Wrong!

00:47:47.340 --> 00:47:49.970
﻿I did go there, but I wasn't infected!

00:47:50.510 --> 00:47:51.340
﻿The rest of my body is—

00:47:59.020 --> 00:48:00.270
﻿Now's the time...

00:48:00.270 --> 00:48:01.350
﻿To take these two down.

00:48:13.870 --> 00:48:15.830
﻿Throw him in the smoking room.

00:48:31.840 --> 00:48:33.180
﻿﻿Don't tell me I'm also...

00:48:49.360 --> 00:48:50.280
﻿﻿Found it!

00:48:57.740 --> 00:49:00.450
﻿Say, aren't those children missing?

00:49:01.040 --> 00:49:01.580
﻿Children?

00:49:02.290 --> 00:49:03.040
﻿Yeah...

00:49:03.710 --> 00:49:07.340
﻿If I recall, there were three boys...

00:49:07.340 --> 00:49:09.090
﻿And another girl about her age.

00:49:10.300 --> 00:49:10.880
﻿Find them.

00:49:12.420 --> 00:49:13.510
﻿Blabbermouth.

00:49:15.090 --> 00:49:18.390
﻿Edogawa-kun, they've discovered that you're missing.

00:49:21.470 --> 00:49:22.350
﻿﻿Edogawa-kun?

00:49:22.770 --> 00:49:23.560
﻿﻿Edogawa-kun!

00:49:24.480 --> 00:49:25.940
﻿Two men were dispatched to find...

00:49:27.770 --> 00:49:28.940
﻿My, how sneaky of you.

00:49:29.480 --> 00:49:30.320
﻿You!

00:49:34.990 --> 00:49:36.410
﻿What are you doing!?

00:49:36.410 --> 00:49:37.820
﻿Are you all right, Ai-chan!?

00:49:38.830 --> 00:49:40.580
﻿Shame on you for slapping a child!

00:49:42.330 --> 00:49:44.290
﻿If you try something like that again...

00:49:44.290 --> 00:49:45.250
﻿I'll kill you.

00:49:49.170 --> 00:49:50.880
﻿Good, got them.

00:50:06.230 --> 00:50:07.940
﻿You guys did this?

00:50:07.940 --> 00:50:09.810
﻿I was the one who did that.

00:50:09.810 --> 00:50:11.480
﻿They had nothing to do with it.

00:50:18.950 --> 00:50:19.910
﻿Such bravery.

00:50:28.670 --> 00:50:29.540
﻿Conan-kun!

00:50:29.670 --> 00:50:30.380
﻿Wait.

00:50:32.210 --> 00:50:32.840
﻿Shinichi...

00:50:44.720 --> 00:50:45.560
Damn!

00:51:00.700 --> 00:51:01.320
﻿All right!

00:51:01.320 --> 00:51:01.910
﻿Kid!

00:51:02.160 --> 00:51:03.620
﻿Nice catch!

00:51:03.740 --> 00:51:05.200
﻿As expected of Kid-sama!

00:51:05.240 --> 00:51:06.750
﻿Great work, even if you are an enemy!

00:51:09.960 --> 00:51:11.420
﻿Shinichi...

00:51:12.500 --> 00:51:14.630
﻿So Kid was here all along.

00:51:14.630 --> 00:51:16.670
﻿At least now all the bothersome parties are gone.

00:51:17.380 --> 00:51:19.430
﻿Reinstall two of the bombs immediately!

00:51:23.260 --> 00:51:26.220
﻿Hard to believe they'd toss you out a window.

00:51:26.220 --> 00:51:27.680
﻿What now, Great Detective?

00:51:28.140 --> 00:51:29.480
﻿Are you giving up like this?

00:51:29.480 --> 00:51:30.850
﻿That's not even an option!

00:51:30.850 --> 00:51:32.190
﻿Return to the airship at once!

00:51:32.440 --> 00:51:34.020
﻿Don't be ridiculous.

00:51:34.020 --> 00:51:37.320
﻿My hang glider doesn't have an engine on it.

00:51:37.320 --> 00:51:39.280
﻿Consider yourself lucky to still be alive!

00:51:41.450 --> 00:51:45.620
﻿Aichi Prefecture Sakushima

00:51:57.510 --> 00:51:59.470
﻿﻿It's headed due west...

00:51:59.800 --> 00:52:02.140
﻿﻿So it's really going toward Osaka?

00:52:02.470 --> 00:52:06.850
Osaka Prefecture Police HQ

00:52:03.340 --> 00:52:07.680
The airship is currently passing above Tsu City, Mie Prefection.

00:52:07.680 --> 00:52:11.350
At this rate, it'll arrive at Osaka in about an hour.

00:52:11.850 --> 00:52:16.270
﻿There's a Bell Tree Tower symbolizing the Suzuki Group in Nankou.

00:52:17.110 --> 00:52:20.030
﻿It's likely the landing port for this test flight.

00:52:21.490 --> 00:52:25.410
﻿Blowing up the airship by crashing it into the tower...

00:52:25.410 --> 00:52:29.950
Is that the plan of the terrorists that hold
﻿a grudge against the Suzuki Group?

00:52:30.500 --> 00:52:32.420
﻿We don't know that for sure.

00:52:32.420 --> 00:52:34.330
﻿If that really comes to be...

00:52:34.330 --> 00:52:36.880
﻿The killer bacteria will spread around right here in Osaka.

00:52:37.500 --> 00:52:41.880
﻿And the lives of seven million Osaka
citizens will be exposed to grave danger.

00:52:42.970 --> 00:52:46.180
﻿We need to prevent that from happening at all costs.

00:52:47.310 --> 00:52:48.760
﻿But what should we do?

00:53:02.030 --> 00:53:02.820
﻿Heiji!

00:53:04.860 --> 00:53:05.620
﻿You're late!

00:53:06.070 --> 00:53:07.530
﻿Sorry, sorry.

00:53:08.120 --> 00:53:09.080
﻿Who's this kid?

00:53:09.950 --> 00:53:10.750
﻿Hello there.

00:53:12.120 --> 00:53:13.620
﻿Kawaguchi Satoshi-kun.

00:53:13.620 --> 00:53:14.580
﻿He's the son of a relative.

00:53:15.290 --> 00:53:17.790
﻿They just moved from Yokohama to Nara this spring.

00:53:17.790 --> 00:53:20.500
﻿And they happened to be visiting my place, so I brought him along.

00:53:21.210 --> 00:53:24.050
﻿Satoshi-kun also said he'd like to meet you.

00:53:24.090 --> 00:53:28.640
﻿See, Heiji, your being good friends with
﻿Conan-kun means you love kids, right?

00:53:28.640 --> 00:53:30.260
﻿Yeah, well...

00:53:30.930 --> 00:53:32.100
﻿Nice to meet you!

00:53:33.390 --> 00:53:34.730
﻿Likewise, nice to meet you.

00:53:35.440 --> 00:53:37.400
﻿Sorry if I sound rude, but...

00:53:37.400 --> 00:53:39.150
﻿Are you two a couple?

00:53:40.730 --> 00:53:41.320
﻿Idiot!

00:53:40.730 --> 00:53:41.780
﻿What are you talking about!?

00:53:41.320 --> 00:53:43.820
﻿Why do I have to be a couple with her?

00:53:41.780 --> 00:53:44.950
Heiji is just my childhood friend, and he's only like a little brother!

00:53:43.860 --> 00:53:45.530
﻿My lover'd look nothing like that!

00:53:44.950 --> 00:53:45.530
﻿Not like that, not like that!

00:53:45.570 --> 00:53:46.450
Impossible, impossible!

00:53:45.570 --> 00:53:46.450
Not like that, not like that!

00:53:47.070 --> 00:53:50.910
﻿In that case, may I take Kazuha-oneesan as my future wife?

00:53:53.040 --> 00:53:54.960
﻿Go ahead, go ahead.

00:53:54.960 --> 00:53:57.420
﻿If you're satisfied with that, I'll even
﻿gift-wrap and hand her over to you.

00:53:57.880 --> 00:53:59.880
﻿Thank you very much, Uncle Heiji!

00:54:00.380 --> 00:54:01.750
﻿Who're you calling "uncle"?

00:54:01.750 --> 00:54:03.800
﻿Now, now, it's just kid's talk.

00:54:04.920 --> 00:54:06.220
﻿Satoshi-kun...

00:54:06.220 --> 00:54:07.890
﻿I'm glad to hear about your feelings, but...

00:54:07.890 --> 00:54:10.350
﻿You have to think hard about that kind of thing.

00:54:11.140 --> 00:54:13.020
﻿For starters, in order to get married...

00:54:13.020 --> 00:54:14.060
﻿I know.

00:54:14.060 --> 00:54:17.350
﻿Boys need to turn eighteen before planning to get married, right?

00:54:17.730 --> 00:54:19.610
Then, let's wait until you're eighteen.

00:54:19.610 --> 00:54:22.780
﻿If you still haven't changed your mind, I'll consider your proposal.

00:54:22.780 --> 00:54:23.110
﻿All right?

00:54:26.360 --> 00:54:27.360
﻿Good!

00:54:27.360 --> 00:54:28.860
﻿We're done with that topic.

00:54:30.160 --> 00:54:32.580
﻿I hope the airship arrives soon!

00:54:32.580 --> 00:54:34.950
﻿Before that, there's a battle against Kid.

00:54:35.750 --> 00:54:37.620
﻿The stage will be above Osaka City.

00:54:37.620 --> 00:54:39.920
﻿I guess we can witness the scene from here.

00:54:40.420 --> 00:54:42.590
﻿This is a premiere ringside seat.

00:54:42.590 --> 00:54:44.920
﻿I love Kid so much!

00:54:44.920 --> 00:54:46.260
﻿We gotta take a photo of him!

00:54:46.260 --> 00:54:47.550
﻿I'm so thrilled about this!

00:54:53.850 --> 00:54:54.640
﻿﻿Kudou?

00:54:56.270 --> 00:54:56.810
﻿Where are you now?

00:54:57.440 --> 00:54:59.690
﻿At Mikawa Bay in Sakushima.

00:54:59.690 --> 00:55:01.810
﻿﻿What, you're still only there?

00:55:02.150 --> 00:55:03.400
﻿It can't be helped.

00:55:03.400 --> 00:55:04.980
﻿I got thrown out.

00:55:04.980 --> 00:55:06.320
﻿﻿Thrown out?

00:55:06.320 --> 00:55:07.650
To be honest, Hattori...{﻿I have a feeling he's planning to take this goat home}

00:55:08.900 --> 00:55:09.860
﻿What was that!?

00:55:12.660 --> 00:55:13.740
﻿Is that for real?

00:55:14.200 --> 00:55:15.240
﻿﻿Yeah.

00:55:15.240 --> 00:55:19.250
﻿﻿The airship carrying the bombs, the killer bacteria, and the hijackers...

00:55:19.250 --> 00:55:20.420
﻿﻿It's coming toward you.

00:55:21.420 --> 00:55:22.630
﻿What a full package.

00:55:23.130 --> 00:55:26.590
﻿Just like the yakisoba okonomiyaki deluxe with
﻿pork, squid, and octopus as triple toppings!

00:55:27.300 --> 00:55:28.970
﻿We already had two people infected.

00:55:29.760 --> 00:55:31.010
﻿Three people.

00:55:31.430 --> 00:55:35.390
﻿That director named Mizukawa also had a rash on his right palm.

00:55:36.520 --> 00:55:37.310
﻿That's how it was.

00:55:38.020 --> 00:55:39.520
﻿﻿I'm just letting you know about this.

00:55:40.730 --> 00:55:42.560
﻿And, are you all right?

00:55:43.650 --> 00:55:44.980
﻿For now, anyway.

00:55:49.530 --> 00:55:51.910
﻿That's a police helicopter.

00:55:52.700 --> 00:55:54.160
﻿Are they chasing the airship?

00:55:56.080 --> 00:55:57.120
﻿﻿Police HQ...

00:55:58.540 --> 00:55:59.540
﻿Sorry, I'll call you back.

00:56:00.000 --> 00:56:01.170
﻿Hey, wait!

00:56:02.420 --> 00:56:04.460
﻿Damn, he hung up again...

00:56:04.500 --> 00:56:05.630
﻿It can't be helped.

00:56:06.630 --> 00:56:09.550
﻿You'd run off to a restaurant once you heard about their great food!

00:56:10.260 --> 00:56:12.970
﻿Weren't you talking about an okonomiyaki restaurant with someone?

00:56:15.140 --> 00:56:16.260
﻿How about it?

00:56:16.260 --> 00:56:17.470
﻿What are their identities?

00:56:18.060 --> 00:56:23.310
﻿About that, we even extended our search
﻿to the relatives of the former leaders...

00:56:23.310 --> 00:56:25.820
﻿But we didn't find anyone that fits the profile.

00:56:26.650 --> 00:56:27.860
﻿It's still no use?

00:56:29.780 --> 00:56:30.900
﻿Megure here.

00:56:30.900 --> 00:56:32.240
﻿﻿Inspector Megure, it's Kudou.

00:56:33.070 --> 00:56:33.700
﻿Kudou-kun!

00:56:34.120 --> 00:56:36.490
﻿I'm currently in Sakushima, Aichi Prefecture.

00:56:37.200 --> 00:56:39.120
﻿But I saw a helicopter from Police HQ chasing that airship.

00:56:39.500 --> 00:56:42.500
﻿Yeah, we have Satou-kun and Takagi-kun en route.

00:56:43.120 --> 00:56:44.460
﻿In fact, Kudou-kun...

00:56:44.460 --> 00:56:46.130
﻿﻿I already know about the hijacking.

00:56:46.670 --> 00:56:48.460
﻿﻿And I'd like to make a request, Inspector.

00:56:49.670 --> 00:56:50.260
﻿What is it?

00:56:50.800 --> 00:56:53.050
﻿Allow me to board that helicopter.

00:56:53.930 --> 00:56:55.340
﻿Me, Kudou Shinichi.

00:57:00.560 --> 00:57:03.520
﻿Hey, where on earth can we find Kudou Shinichi?

00:57:03.520 --> 00:57:04.980
﻿Given that you <i>are</i> Kudou Shinichi.

00:57:05.440 --> 00:57:07.650
As-I-said...

00:57:07.650 --> 00:57:09.650
﻿I'm asking you to disguise as me!

00:57:11.030 --> 00:57:12.700
﻿I have to disguise as you again?

00:57:13.740 --> 00:57:14.660
﻿Oh, nothing.

00:57:15.450 --> 00:57:18.910
﻿I can lend you a hand, but you can't interfere with my job.

00:57:18.950 --> 00:57:20.700
﻿I can't make any promises, but...

00:57:21.330 --> 00:57:22.710
﻿I'll see what I can do.

00:57:31.090 --> 00:57:31.670
﻿Good.

00:57:32.420 --> 00:57:34.680
﻿Cat-E, start the preparations.

00:57:35.220 --> 00:57:35.760
﻿Roger.

00:57:37.680 --> 00:57:38.390
﻿What?

00:57:39.140 --> 00:57:40.560
﻿What are you up to now?

00:57:45.980 --> 00:57:47.690
﻿It's been a while, Kudou-kun.

00:57:47.690 --> 00:57:48.190
﻿Same here.

00:57:48.860 --> 00:57:52.030
﻿But I'm surprised to see Conan-kun here as well.

00:57:53.280 --> 00:57:55.280
﻿What were you doing in Sakushima?

00:57:55.820 --> 00:57:57.450
﻿I'll explain everything later.

00:57:57.450 --> 00:57:58.950
﻿For now, please pursue the airship.

00:57:59.990 --> 00:58:00.660
﻿Pursue the airship.

00:58:10.630 --> 00:58:11.300
There it is.

00:58:11.460 --> 00:58:12.550
﻿It's the airship.

00:58:14.300 --> 00:58:15.760
﻿Please approach it.

00:58:15.760 --> 00:58:18.930
﻿In order to avoid drawing the criminals'
﻿attention, please elevate adequately.

00:58:18.930 --> 00:58:19.430
Roger.

00:58:24.310 --> 00:58:27.020
﻿What's the direction of the wind and the speed of the helicopter?

00:58:27.020 --> 00:58:28.940
﻿Southeast, 200 kilometers per hour.

00:58:29.810 --> 00:58:32.270
﻿Continue straight ahead and once you overtake the airship...

00:58:32.270 --> 00:58:34.320
﻿Please maintain the same speed.

00:58:34.820 --> 00:58:35.820
﻿Kudou-kun?

00:58:47.830 --> 00:58:49.750
﻿Kudou-kun, what on earth...

00:58:51.290 --> 00:58:53.960
﻿All right then, please excuse us.

00:58:59.970 --> 00:59:00.550
﻿Kid?

00:59:14.230 --> 00:59:15.440
﻿The wings, the wings!

00:59:15.440 --> 00:59:16.650
﻿The wings!

00:59:16.650 --> 00:59:18.200
﻿Fold your wings!

00:59:18.400 --> 00:59:19.780
﻿Hurry and fold your wings!

00:59:20.200 --> 00:59:22.410
﻿I can't press the switch with you in the way!

00:59:22.830 --> 00:59:23.490
﻿Damn...

00:59:25.040 --> 00:59:26.500
﻿Hey, where are you touching?

00:59:27.410 --> 00:59:28.040
﻿Stop it...

00:59:28.040 --> 00:59:30.120
﻿Don't move, I'm trying to press the switch!

00:59:30.580 --> 00:59:31.880
﻿Even if you say so, it tickles!

00:59:31.880 --> 00:59:32.710
﻿Bear with it!

00:59:32.920 --> 00:59:33.880
﻿Hey, that's my...

00:59:38.550 --> 00:59:39.470
﻿Look out!

00:59:50.890 --> 00:59:51.520
﻿Retreat!

00:59:58.740 --> 01:00:00.700
﻿Then, that means, Kudou-kun is...

01:00:00.700 --> 01:00:01.610
﻿Actually Kid?

01:00:13.710 --> 01:00:15.880
﻿Well then, I bid you good luck.

01:00:16.590 --> 01:00:17.880
﻿You're not coming along?

01:00:19.800 --> 01:00:22.130
﻿I'll be checking on the situation here for a while.

01:00:23.180 --> 01:00:25.890
﻿After all, the gem's already fallen into the leader's hands.

01:00:25.890 --> 01:00:26.720
﻿Oh, yeah.

01:00:28.060 --> 01:00:28.520
﻿Catch.

01:00:30.730 --> 01:00:31.850
﻿What's this?

01:00:32.600 --> 01:00:34.690
﻿Old Jirokichi's fingerprint seal.

01:00:36.480 --> 01:00:37.650
﻿Thank you.

01:00:43.660 --> 01:00:48.120
﻿Although I correctly guessed the glass case would be
﻿protected by a fingerprint authorization system...

01:00:50.040 --> 01:00:52.000
﻿I have no use for it anymore, so I'm entrusting it to you.

01:00:52.670 --> 01:00:54.710
﻿By the way, about your important girlfriend...

01:00:55.380 --> 01:00:56.880
﻿It's best that you keep an eye on her.

01:00:58.380 --> 01:01:01.760
﻿That man Fujioka grabbed both her arms earlier.

01:01:02.470 --> 01:01:04.220
﻿She did push him away quickly, though.

01:01:04.720 --> 01:01:08.970
﻿Since it wasn't via coughing or sneezing, I don't think she's infected.

01:01:09.350 --> 01:01:11.310
﻿Just thought I'd let you know.

01:01:30.620 --> 01:01:31.370
﻿Nothing...

01:01:33.500 --> 01:01:36.250
﻿﻿I thought they would've reinstalled one here for sure...

01:01:39.590 --> 01:01:40.960
﻿﻿There isn't one here either.

01:01:41.340 --> 01:01:44.470
﻿Could it be that they planted them in different places?

01:01:52.560 --> 01:01:55.230
﻿In the end, I only found two.

01:01:56.560 --> 01:02:00.730
﻿﻿And they were in the exact same places
﻿where Genta and Mitsuhiko had found them.

01:02:01.440 --> 01:02:02.110
﻿﻿Why?

01:02:02.780 --> 01:02:06.780
﻿Why didn't they reattach them to the
﻿places that would release the bacteria?

01:02:08.200 --> 01:02:10.080
﻿At any rate, I need to disarm them.

01:02:14.200 --> 01:02:15.160
﻿Hey, Kudou!

01:02:15.500 --> 01:02:18.920
﻿You said you'd call me back, but you totally didn't!

01:02:19.170 --> 01:02:19.670
﻿Kudou?

01:02:20.420 --> 01:02:21.380
I mean...

01:02:21.380 --> 01:02:22.340
﻿Cool down, Conan-kun.

01:02:22.800 --> 01:02:25.260
﻿My bad, my bad, I completely forgot.

01:02:25.260 --> 01:02:26.260
﻿Geez...

01:02:26.260 --> 01:02:27.840
﻿﻿Where the hell are you now?

01:02:28.220 --> 01:02:29.300
﻿Inside the airship.

01:02:29.680 --> 01:02:30.850
﻿You already went back?

01:02:31.470 --> 01:02:32.890
﻿Pretty nimble, aren't ya?

01:02:33.560 --> 01:02:35.060
﻿Regardless, what's this about?

01:02:35.060 --> 01:02:36.560
﻿I'm a little busy.

01:02:37.560 --> 01:02:40.560
﻿The culprits spread the news about the airship on the internet...

01:02:40.560 --> 01:02:42.780
﻿All of Osaka's in a state of panic.

01:02:43.230 --> 01:02:43.610
﻿What!?

01:02:44.320 --> 01:02:48.450
The bullet train station is jam-packed with
 ﻿people trying to escape Osaka to the west.

01:02:48.660 --> 01:02:50.410
﻿Like I said, we're out of seats!

01:02:50.410 --> 01:02:51.200
﻿If it's to Tokyo...

01:02:51.240 --> 01:02:52.870
﻿Idiot, why can it go to that dangerous place!?

01:02:53.120 --> 01:02:54.540
There will be another train coming!

01:02:54.830 --> 01:02:55.750
﻿Please don't push!

01:02:55.750 --> 01:02:57.160
﻿Why, when there's still space to fit in!?

01:02:57.160 --> 01:02:58.250
﻿Please board the next train!

01:03:12.260 --> 01:03:16.060
﻿Even the highway and local roads are congested
﻿with cars leaving Osaka bound westward.

01:03:16.890 --> 01:03:20.980
﻿Not to mention bank employees and
﻿security guards have all evacuated.

01:03:21.810 --> 01:03:23.520
﻿Now'd be a great time to rob a bank, huh?

01:03:24.360 --> 01:03:26.280
﻿I think it's best not to do that.

01:03:26.280 --> 01:03:28.650
﻿Security systems nowadays are pretty tight.

01:03:28.990 --> 01:03:30.700
It's a joke, a joke.

01:03:30.700 --> 01:03:32.530
﻿Don't interrupt when adults are talking.

01:03:33.160 --> 01:03:34.280
﻿Security...

01:03:34.740 --> 01:03:35.290
﻿Hey.

01:03:37.250 --> 01:03:38.250
﻿What the...

01:03:38.250 --> 01:03:39.120
﻿Don't scare me.

01:03:40.000 --> 01:03:41.460
﻿I saw something interesting.

01:03:42.920 --> 01:03:44.380
﻿Sorry, I'll call you back.

01:03:45.300 --> 01:03:46.050
﻿Hey!

01:03:46.590 --> 01:03:47.840
﻿Damn, he did it again.

01:03:48.510 --> 01:03:49.720
﻿What's with him?

01:03:50.130 --> 01:03:51.720
﻿Say, Kazuha-oneesan?

01:03:52.800 --> 01:03:53.180
﻿What?

01:03:53.800 --> 01:03:56.600
﻿Who was Uncle Heiji talking to just now?

01:03:58.270 --> 01:03:59.520
﻿It's Conan-kun.

01:03:59.520 --> 01:04:00.270
﻿Conan-kun?

01:04:01.190 --> 01:04:05.360
He's about your age, an elementary school student who's really smart.

01:04:05.360 --> 01:04:07.780
﻿He always hit it off well with Heiji.

01:04:08.070 --> 01:04:09.570
﻿Then, what did he mean by "when adults are—"

01:04:09.610 --> 01:04:10.070
﻿Hey!

01:04:10.990 --> 01:04:12.820
﻿Don't go blabbering idle talk!

01:04:13.280 --> 01:04:16.120
﻿Fine, fine, it was my bad...

01:04:16.120 --> 01:04:17.580
﻿Uncle Heiji!

01:04:23.790 --> 01:04:24.630
﻿What is it?

01:04:24.630 --> 01:04:25.750
﻿This "something interesting".

01:04:39.100 --> 01:04:40.310
﻿Rocket flares?

01:04:40.770 --> 01:04:42.020
﻿What's this about?

01:04:50.740 --> 01:04:52.490
﻿We'll reach Nara once we pass this mountain.

01:04:52.990 --> 01:04:57.240
﻿With the airship smoking like this, people
﻿in Nara will certainly be surprised, huh?

01:04:57.990 --> 01:04:59.790
﻿They won't just be surprised!

01:05:01.200 --> 01:05:02.000
﻿Panic?

01:05:02.290 --> 01:05:06.790
﻿Those guys already posted the news about
﻿the bacteria and the bombs on the internet.

01:05:07.630 --> 01:05:10.130
﻿At the moment, everyone's being evacuated, and...

01:05:10.170 --> 01:05:10.800
﻿Yeah.

01:05:11.260 --> 01:05:13.260
﻿If Nara is like that too...

01:05:13.260 --> 01:05:15.680
﻿It'll be a lucky break for thieves.

01:05:15.680 --> 01:05:16.890
﻿Idiot.

01:05:16.890 --> 01:05:19.890
﻿Even if there's no people, nowadays the security systems...

01:05:21.180 --> 01:05:22.180
﻿Security?

01:05:24.230 --> 01:05:25.190
﻿Don't tell me...

01:05:25.190 --> 01:05:26.310
﻿That's why they chose Nara?

01:05:27.270 --> 01:05:28.770
﻿Certainly a possibility.

01:05:29.440 --> 01:05:30.320
But...

01:05:30.690 --> 01:05:32.530
﻿﻿If that's true, why did they...

01:05:33.490 --> 01:05:35.410
﻿Prepare bacteria just for this?

01:05:38.620 --> 01:05:39.280
I see.

01:05:39.620 --> 01:05:40.330
﻿All right, got it.

01:05:41.040 --> 01:05:42.290
﻿You can count on me.

01:05:43.460 --> 01:05:44.750
﻿Where are you going, Heiji?

01:05:45.330 --> 01:05:46.460
﻿Nara, Nara.

01:05:46.460 --> 01:05:47.170
﻿Nara?

01:05:47.540 --> 01:05:51.090
﻿If it's Nara, is it related to that airship?

01:05:51.670 --> 01:05:53.760
﻿Yeah, and it's dangerous, so don't tag along.

01:05:54.420 --> 01:05:55.720
﻿Please take me with you!

01:05:55.930 --> 01:05:58.890
﻿Idiot, I just told you not to come along!

01:05:58.890 --> 01:06:01.850
﻿I know Nara's roads very well, so I'll be a big help!

01:06:01.850 --> 01:06:02.930
﻿I'm going too!

01:06:02.930 --> 01:06:04.810
﻿What are you talking about now?

01:06:05.230 --> 01:06:07.850
﻿First of all, three people on a bike is illegal...

01:06:07.850 --> 01:06:08.810
﻿Don't worry, don't worry!

01:06:09.480 --> 01:06:11.270
﻿I just thought of a great plan.

01:06:13.440 --> 01:06:14.990
﻿Hold on tight!

01:06:14.990 --> 01:06:15.860
﻿Got it!

01:06:16.320 --> 01:06:18.370
﻿Satoshi-kun, are you all right?

01:06:19.070 --> 01:06:20.370
﻿Yeah, I'm fine.

01:06:20.370 --> 01:06:22.290
﻿We'll arrive there soon, so please hang on.

01:06:22.950 --> 01:06:24.750
﻿﻿Are you sure this is really all right?

01:06:36.470 --> 01:06:37.470
﻿﻿It can't be...

01:06:37.470 --> 01:06:38.300
﻿﻿Why?

01:06:52.770 --> 01:06:53.360
﻿Ran!

01:06:59.700 --> 01:07:00.070
﻿Ran!

01:07:00.780 --> 01:07:01.910
﻿Ran!

01:07:01.910 --> 01:07:02.490
﻿Sit down!

01:07:09.210 --> 01:07:09.960
Ran...

01:07:25.310 --> 01:07:26.350
﻿Rashes...

01:07:35.480 --> 01:07:36.490
﻿Help me!

01:07:36.490 --> 01:07:37.280
﻿Please!

01:07:38.450 --> 01:07:39.240
Let go!

01:07:40.490 --> 01:07:42.200
﻿Hey, you get in too!

01:07:42.200 --> 01:07:43.330
﻿Don't touch me!

01:07:48.540 --> 01:07:50.000
﻿Damn...

01:08:04.720 --> 01:08:06.010
﻿What does this mean?

01:08:06.600 --> 01:08:10.060
﻿As Kid said, infection won't occur merely by touching one's arms.

01:08:10.690 --> 01:08:12.480
﻿Not only did Ran shove him away...

01:08:12.480 --> 01:08:14.770
﻿Fujioka-san didn't cough or sneeze.

01:08:16.730 --> 01:08:20.240
﻿﻿On the other hand, Genta was sneezed on...

01:08:20.240 --> 01:08:23.950
﻿And even breathed in the bacteria in the ﻿smoking room, but still wasn't infected.

01:08:24.160 --> 01:08:24.700
﻿Why is that?

01:08:28.330 --> 01:08:31.920
﻿That director named Mizukawa also had rashes on his right palm.

01:08:36.710 --> 01:08:37.710
Could it be...

01:08:47.720 --> 01:08:49.470
﻿The airship is after us!

01:08:49.520 --> 01:08:50.270
﻿The bacteria!

01:08:50.270 --> 01:08:51.480
﻿The bacteria is pouring down!

01:08:51.690 --> 01:08:53.440
﻿It's jam-packed with bombs!

01:09:01.860 --> 01:09:05.530
﻿Goufuku Temple

01:09:02.150 --> 01:09:04.110
Everything's on standby!

01:09:04.110 --> 01:09:05.370
Hurry, hurry!

01:09:05.370 --> 01:09:06.740
Hurry up and evacuate!

01:09:08.290 --> 01:09:10.120
﻿But the Buddhas...

01:09:10.160 --> 01:09:13.250
﻿The Buddhas will not be infected by bacteria!

01:09:13.250 --> 01:09:14.670
﻿Hurry up and get in the vehicle!

01:09:14.830 --> 01:09:15.670
﻿What if they punish us...

01:09:15.670 --> 01:09:17.090
﻿We'll come back, don't worry!

01:09:17.090 --> 01:09:18.130
﻿Just get in!

01:09:29.350 --> 01:09:30.140
Ran...

01:09:30.970 --> 01:09:32.270
﻿Ran-oneesan...

01:09:35.440 --> 01:09:35.940
﻿Go check it out.

01:09:56.120 --> 01:09:56.710
﻿Hey!

01:09:58.880 --> 01:09:59.380
﻿You...

01:10:03.130 --> 01:10:03.550
﻿Cat-A?

01:10:05.720 --> 01:10:06.760
﻿Cat-A, what's wrong?

01:10:06.800 --> 01:10:07.340
﻿Respond!

01:10:10.600 --> 01:10:11.560
﻿Go check the situation!

01:10:26.740 --> 01:10:27.450
﻿Hey!

01:10:27.450 --> 01:10:28.070
﻿What's wrong?

01:10:29.030 --> 01:10:29.530
﻿Hey!

01:10:32.830 --> 01:10:34.040
﻿He's asleep?

01:10:46.010 --> 01:10:46.590
Cat-B!

01:10:47.010 --> 01:10:47.840
﻿﻿What's wrong?

01:10:47.840 --> 01:10:48.430
﻿﻿Something happen?

01:10:48.930 --> 01:10:49.550
﻿﻿Cat-B!

01:10:50.140 --> 01:10:52.850
﻿If it's about Cat-B, he's out cold on the roof.

01:10:53.310 --> 01:10:54.680
﻿Which is strange...

01:10:54.680 --> 01:10:56.810
﻿Since cats shouldn't land on their backs.

01:10:57.440 --> 01:10:58.270
﻿It's Conan!

01:10:58.310 --> 01:10:59.400
﻿So he did come back!

01:10:59.770 --> 01:11:01.020
﻿With Kid-san, right?

01:11:01.520 --> 01:11:02.860
﻿Kid-san isn't here.

01:11:02.980 --> 01:11:03.860
Damn!

01:11:04.190 --> 01:11:05.990
﻿Cat-C, D, E:

01:11:05.990 --> 01:11:07.240
﻿Go capture that brat!

01:11:07.990 --> 01:11:08.990
﻿No...

01:11:08.990 --> 01:11:10.950
﻿Once you find him, open fire.

01:11:11.660 --> 01:11:13.370
﻿Roger.

01:11:13.950 --> 01:11:15.580
﻿You go guard the dining room.

01:11:16.660 --> 01:11:17.210
C﻿at-F!

01:11:17.710 --> 01:11:18.250
﻿Roger.

01:11:20.630 --> 01:11:23.340
﻿I'll head there once I've switched to autopilot!

01:12:14.300 --> 01:12:14.890
﻿Damn it!

01:12:36.580 --> 01:12:37.290
Damn!

01:12:56.260 --> 01:12:57.760
﻿The brat's gone up to the sky deck!

01:13:22.040 --> 01:13:22.710
﻿One, and...

01:13:25.130 --> 01:13:25.500
﻿Seven!

01:13:31.800 --> 01:13:34.010
﻿The trap set for Kid came in handy.

01:13:34.880 --> 01:13:35.930
﻿And this too.

01:13:37.800 --> 01:13:38.810
﻿W﻿ait a minute...

01:13:39.640 --> 01:13:41.890
﻿Did he do this on purpose so I could use it?

01:13:42.770 --> 01:13:43.270
﻿Don't move!

01:13:45.690 --> 01:13:46.810
﻿Throw that away.

01:13:48.230 --> 01:13:49.770
﻿Keep your hands in the air.

01:13:51.480 --> 01:13:52.820
﻿I saw everything.

01:13:52.820 --> 01:13:54.740
﻿You're really something, aren't you?

01:13:55.490 --> 01:13:56.990
﻿Now, put your hands on that!

01:13:58.320 --> 01:13:59.160
﻿You sure you want that?

01:13:59.490 --> 01:14:01.080
﻿Don't defy me.

01:14:01.120 --> 01:14:01.490
Yes, sir...

01:14:02.080 --> 01:14:04.250
﻿I'm not like the others who...

01:14:09.340 --> 01:14:10.300
﻿Can't say I didn't warn you.

01:14:12.050 --> 01:14:13.050
﻿Damn you!

01:14:26.980 --> 01:14:27.940
﻿Hey, hey...

01:14:27.940 --> 01:14:28.980
﻿Are you serious?

01:14:32.030 --> 01:14:32.820
﻿What is all this?

01:14:33.280 --> 01:14:36.950
﻿The third trap Uncle Jirokichi set up just for you.

01:14:37.660 --> 01:14:39.070
﻿Is that so?

01:14:39.070 --> 01:14:40.410
﻿If I stole the jewel...

01:14:41.120 --> 01:14:43.950
﻿And escaped from that hole by firing my grappling hook...

01:14:45.910 --> 01:14:47.250
﻿That was a close one!

01:14:48.210 --> 01:14:49.380
﻿He's one hell of an old guy.

01:14:49.920 --> 01:14:51.130
﻿And hey, you...

01:14:51.750 --> 01:14:53.340
﻿Were you up here this whole time?

01:15:14.730 --> 01:15:15.530
﻿Take this!

01:15:31.790 --> 01:15:32.840
﻿You're good.

01:15:37.510 --> 01:15:38.760
And here's...

01:15:39.380 --> 01:15:40.430
﻿A warrior's medal.

01:15:44.350 --> 01:15:45.810
﻿﻿Are the rest of you listening?

01:15:46.810 --> 01:15:48.770
﻿﻿I've taken out your leader.

01:15:48.770 --> 01:15:49.980
﻿﻿Along with the other three.

01:15:50.560 --> 01:15:50.940
﻿What?

01:15:51.560 --> 01:15:52.440
﻿Don't fool around.

01:15:53.900 --> 01:15:55.150
﻿Go, Lupin!

01:16:12.580 --> 01:16:13.380
﻿We did it!

01:16:13.840 --> 01:16:14.880
﻿Geez.

01:16:14.880 --> 01:16:16.340
﻿Don't wave this thing around carelessly!

01:16:18.670 --> 01:16:20.050
﻿Edogawa-kun!

01:16:20.090 --> 01:16:21.470
﻿We've disabled the two here as well.

01:16:22.090 --> 01:16:22.800
﻿Roger that.

01:16:32.940 --> 01:16:35.320
﻿What an impressive number of records.

01:16:35.820 --> 01:16:38.070
﻿Moreover, within the last two to three hours...

01:16:38.940 --> 01:16:40.780
﻿Hey, who'd you call?

01:16:41.240 --> 01:16:42.700
﻿And so many times.

01:16:45.160 --> 01:16:46.620
﻿If you don't wanna talk...

01:16:48.330 --> 01:16:49.950
﻿What do you plan to do with that?

01:16:50.460 --> 01:16:52.960
﻿If you don't confess...

01:16:52.960 --> 01:16:54.920
﻿I figure I'll pour the contents all over you.

01:16:57.960 --> 01:16:58.840
﻿Do what you want.

01:17:15.270 --> 01:17:16.400
﻿Put it down for a while.

01:17:17.070 --> 01:17:18.110
﻿Slowly...

01:17:21.650 --> 01:17:22.780
﻿I see.

01:17:23.700 --> 01:17:25.450
﻿This is one neat plan.

01:17:26.160 --> 01:17:29.330
﻿The bioterrorist attack on the airship was just a diversion.

01:17:29.790 --> 01:17:38.000
Your real intention was to evacuate everyone and steal the
 ﻿nationally-protected Buddha statues from the empty temple.

01:17:38.540 --> 01:17:42.170
﻿Temples usually don't have security systems
 ﻿so you guys counted on that, didn't you?

01:17:42.760 --> 01:17:46.890
﻿Normally, no one would think of stealing Buddha statues.

01:17:46.890 --> 01:17:48.140
﻿You have sinned!

01:17:48.640 --> 01:17:50.220
﻿What are you talking about?

01:17:50.220 --> 01:17:52.480
﻿We just wanted to protect the Buddha statues.

01:17:52.480 --> 01:17:54.980
﻿If that's so, share with us the name of one Nara police inspector.

01:17:55.650 --> 01:17:57.360
﻿Anyone'll do—give it a try.

01:17:58.110 --> 01:17:58.860
That's...

01:17:59.110 --> 01:18:00.020
﻿What's this?

01:18:00.020 --> 01:18:01.610
﻿You can't even come up with one?

01:18:01.610 --> 01:18:03.440
﻿Being a police officer, that's strange.

01:18:03.440 --> 01:18:05.240
﻿Hey, there was one.

01:18:05.240 --> 01:18:07.620
﻿A police inspector with a name that suits Nara.

01:18:08.660 --> 01:18:10.160
﻿They're just a bunch of kids.

01:18:10.200 --> 01:18:10.910
﻿Do it.

01:18:11.740 --> 01:18:12.830
﻿Hello?

01:18:12.830 --> 01:18:14.500
﻿What'd you just say?

01:18:14.500 --> 01:18:16.750
﻿They said we're just a bunch of kids.

01:18:16.830 --> 01:18:17.960
﻿What's that?

01:18:17.960 --> 01:18:19.540
﻿They're idiots, aren't they?

01:18:20.460 --> 01:18:21.800
﻿Definitely.

01:18:21.800 --> 01:18:23.800
﻿How can there be only three of us...

01:18:23.800 --> 01:18:26.470
﻿When we're here to catch a group of thieves?

01:18:26.470 --> 01:18:26.970
﻿What!?

01:18:27.930 --> 01:18:28.890
Damn!

01:18:30.260 --> 01:18:33.520
﻿This is the Nara Prefecture Investigation Third Section Inspector...

01:18:34.100 --> 01:18:38.020
﻿Shikatsuno Tsuyoshi

01:18:34.100 --> 01:18:38.020
﻿Nara Police Officer

01:18:34.230 --> 01:18:35.310
Shikatsuno Tsuyoshi!

01:18:35.440 --> 01:18:37.020
Remember my words:

01:18:37.020 --> 01:18:39.520
Never belittle the Nara police!

01:18:43.570 --> 01:18:44.440
﻿Yo, Kudou.

01:18:44.780 --> 01:18:47.860
﻿﻿All the thieves after the Buddha statues have been apprehended.

01:18:48.450 --> 01:18:51.030
﻿﻿Of course, all the abbots are safe as well.

01:18:51.370 --> 01:18:52.410
﻿Got it.

01:18:52.450 --> 01:18:53.830
﻿Thanks, Heiji-niichan.

01:18:54.330 --> 01:18:55.580
﻿Geez...

01:18:55.620 --> 01:18:58.750
﻿As expected, that boy detective from Osaka pulled some strings.

01:19:00.170 --> 01:19:01.750
﻿To say "pulling strings"...

01:19:01.960 --> 01:19:02.630
﻿Oh, that's right.

01:19:04.340 --> 01:19:05.010
﻿Here's this.

01:19:06.970 --> 01:19:08.630
﻿Thank you, lad.

01:19:08.630 --> 01:19:11.640
﻿That aside, we have to take Ran to a hospital immediately!

01:19:11.640 --> 01:19:12.390
﻿Oh, right.

01:19:12.970 --> 01:19:14.140
﻿About that...

01:19:23.520 --> 01:19:25.490
﻿I don't want to die...

01:19:29.450 --> 01:19:30.450
﻿Ran-neechan?

01:19:33.870 --> 01:19:35.290
﻿Conan-kun!

01:19:35.790 --> 01:19:36.540
﻿Don't!

01:19:36.540 --> 01:19:37.750
﻿Don't come near me, Conan-kun!

01:19:38.290 --> 01:19:40.500
﻿It's all right, Ran-neechan.

01:19:40.540 --> 01:19:43.380
﻿Because no one was infected at all.

01:19:45.340 --> 01:19:46.420
﻿But, the rashes...

01:19:47.170 --> 01:19:49.590
﻿Those rashes are merely the result of skin irritation.

01:19:49.590 --> 01:19:51.890
﻿Probably just a reaction from contact with lacquer.

01:19:51.890 --> 01:19:52.600
﻿Lacquer?

01:19:53.100 --> 01:19:55.890
﻿The person who brought Ran-neechan here earlier.

01:19:55.930 --> 01:19:58.310
﻿It was the same one who escorted Mizukawa-san as well, right?

01:19:59.100 --> 01:19:59.520
﻿Yeah...

01:19:59.980 --> 01:20:00.850
﻿I knew it.

01:20:01.350 --> 01:20:05.110
﻿Among all the people, he's the only one resistant to lacquer.

01:20:06.320 --> 01:20:08.320
﻿Given that his fingernails have turned black...

01:20:09.280 --> 01:20:12.370
﻿He's likely a former lacquer craftsman of some sort.

01:20:14.410 --> 01:20:18.500
﻿In other words, the culprits didn't steal any bacteria in the first place.

01:20:19.500 --> 01:20:20.960
﻿They only blew up the laboratory...

01:20:21.710 --> 01:20:24.880
﻿To make this biochemical terrorist act seem real.

01:20:26.590 --> 01:20:28.460
﻿This ampule is the evidence.

01:20:29.550 --> 01:20:33.390
﻿I acted as if I were going to open this in front of their leader, but...

01:20:33.390 --> 01:20:36.100
﻿He didn't even do so much as flinch.

01:20:36.760 --> 01:20:39.060
﻿If there was really bacteria inside...

01:20:39.060 --> 01:20:40.520
﻿He would've tried his hardest to stop me.

01:20:41.020 --> 01:20:43.650
﻿Just like how Ran-neechan asked me to stay away just now.

01:20:44.610 --> 01:20:45.440
﻿Conan-kun...

01:20:46.270 --> 01:20:47.820
﻿Isn't that right, Uncle?

01:20:48.530 --> 01:20:49.320
﻿Yeah...

01:20:49.780 --> 01:20:50.820
﻿Are you all right, Ran?

01:20:52.490 --> 01:20:53.320
﻿Moreover, look.

01:20:53.910 --> 01:20:55.780
﻿Apart from the rashes that appeared initially...

01:20:55.780 --> 01:20:58.620
﻿They've also appeared on your hands, arms, and...

01:20:58.660 --> 01:21:01.250
﻿The back of your legs, right?

01:21:02.000 --> 01:21:02.540
﻿No way!

01:21:03.330 --> 01:21:08.380
﻿I'm sure the culprits sprayed lacquer all over this room.

01:21:08.920 --> 01:21:11.470
﻿The walls, the sofa, the door handle, and everything.

01:21:12.720 --> 01:21:14.930
﻿That's why, for Ran-neechan...

01:21:14.930 --> 01:21:20.310
The rashes on your arms were caused by Fujioka-san's
﻿grabbing, who came to smoke and touched lacquer.

01:21:20.640 --> 01:21:25.940
The rashes on the rest of your body were only
﻿caused by coming into contact with lacquer in this...

01:21:25.940 --> 01:21:26.610
﻿Room...

01:21:27.900 --> 01:21:28.570
﻿﻿Hold on!

01:21:29.230 --> 01:21:30.280
﻿﻿Then, why was that person...

01:21:34.450 --> 01:21:34.820
﻿Hey!

01:21:35.280 --> 01:21:35.700
﻿What's wrong?

01:21:36.410 --> 01:21:37.660
﻿Conan-kun...

01:21:52.470 --> 01:21:53.550
﻿Damn it!

01:22:00.770 --> 01:22:02.930
﻿Based on the information from Nara prefecture...

01:22:02.930 --> 01:22:04.890
﻿We've uncovered the true identities of the hijacking group.

01:22:05.900 --> 01:22:08.650
﻿They appear to be experienced foreign mercenaries.

01:22:09.230 --> 01:22:10.480
﻿Mercenaries?

01:22:10.860 --> 01:22:12.940
﻿Then, their claim about being the Red Siamese Cats...

01:22:13.570 --> 01:22:15.610
﻿It's completely unrelated.

01:22:15.610 --> 01:22:18.070
﻿They made use of that terrorist organization's name...

01:22:18.070 --> 01:22:21.240
﻿In order to camouflage their true aim of stealing Buddha statues.

01:22:21.950 --> 01:22:25.460
﻿And the person who recruited them this time is...

01:22:48.440 --> 01:22:49.310
﻿Hold it.

01:22:50.310 --> 01:22:53.230
﻿To leave your subordinates behind and escape alone...

01:22:53.230 --> 01:22:54.990
﻿Don’t you find that a little cowardly?

01:22:55.950 --> 01:22:57.990
Boss of hijacking group...

01:22:58.610 --> 01:23:00.200
﻿Fujioka Takamichi-san?

01:23:01.370 --> 01:23:02.620
﻿Boy...

01:23:02.620 --> 01:23:04.700
﻿Well done in figuring out my true identity.

01:23:05.040 --> 01:23:06.290
﻿Nah.

01:23:06.290 --> 01:23:11.170
﻿I was completely deceived when you
 ﻿pretended to be the person first infected.

01:23:11.920 --> 01:23:14.460
Probably, right after the airship took off...

01:23:14.460 --> 01:23:18.220
That female subordinate-oft ours
 ﻿sprayed lacquer in the smoking room...

01:23:18.510 --> 01:23:19.840
﻿And left the ampule there.

01:23:22.140 --> 01:23:24.220
﻿Undoubtedly, this was per your instruction.

01:23:25.060 --> 01:23:29.190
Afterward, you entered the smoking room and
 ﻿came into contact with the lacquer on purpose...

01:23:29.900 --> 01:23:33.860
﻿In order to convince us that you were the
﻿first person infected with the bacteria.

01:23:34.730 --> 01:23:38.900
﻿On the sky deck, you invited Uncle Kogorou to the smoking room...

01:23:39.740 --> 01:23:41.530
﻿﻿Mouri-san, how about it?

01:23:42.370 --> 01:23:44.120
﻿And grabbed Ran's arms...

01:23:46.080 --> 01:23:49.000
﻿To "infect" all the people who could pose a threat...

01:23:49.000 --> 01:23:50.580
﻿And prevent them from getting in your way.

01:23:51.380 --> 01:23:54.340
﻿But, it didn't go over very well with Uncle, so...

01:23:54.340 --> 01:23:56.800
﻿All you had to do was put sleeping pills in his beer!

01:23:57.380 --> 01:23:59.430
﻿Thanks to you, he was sound asleep until now.

01:24:01.430 --> 01:24:06.140
﻿For Mizukawa-san and the waitress, the rashes
﻿appeared on their palms and the back of their arms...

01:24:06.850 --> 01:24:09.230
﻿Which were likely the result of them
﻿touching something in the smoking room.

01:24:09.730 --> 01:24:11.270
﻿Genta, on the other hand...

01:24:11.310 --> 01:24:15.780
﻿Didn't get the rashes because he only peeked
﻿inside there without touching anything.

01:24:16.360 --> 01:24:18.280
﻿In other words, you were the only person.

01:24:19.110 --> 01:24:22.320
﻿Only you had rashes on your neck and face—places
﻿usually unlikely to come into contact with anything.

01:24:23.030 --> 01:24:26.580
﻿Moreover, the leader was constantly
﻿talking to someone on his cellphone.

01:24:28.580 --> 01:24:29.910
﻿That's how I knew...

01:24:30.710 --> 01:24:36.130
﻿That you used the lacquer from the smoking room and
﻿smeared it on yourself in order to induce the rashes.

01:24:36.130 --> 01:24:38.170
﻿You made use of the bacteria infection scare...

01:24:38.510 --> 01:24:44.100
﻿In order to isolate yourself and give orders to
﻿the terrorist group when no one was looking...

01:24:45.140 --> 01:24:47.100
﻿You were the big boss!

01:24:49.430 --> 01:24:51.980
﻿That's quite a brilliant deduction, brat.

01:24:52.690 --> 01:24:55.150
﻿However, you omitted something of great importance.

01:24:55.480 --> 01:24:56.270
﻿What?

01:24:57.110 --> 01:25:00.650
﻿I had no intention of escaping alone in the first place.

01:25:01.150 --> 01:25:03.660
﻿Unfortunately, all your subordinates have been...

01:25:03.660 --> 01:25:04.740
﻿I don't mean them.

01:25:05.490 --> 01:25:07.330
﻿Not those that I hired.

01:25:08.120 --> 01:25:09.790
﻿I mean my original subordinates.

01:25:11.160 --> 01:25:12.210
﻿Don’t tell me, there are others!?

01:25:13.920 --> 01:25:15.040
﻿Don't move!

01:25:16.380 --> 01:25:17.090
﻿Sonoko!

01:25:19.170 --> 01:25:20.710
﻿We told you not to move, didn't we?

01:25:22.260 --> 01:25:23.260
﻿Edogawa-kun...

01:25:23.260 --> 01:25:24.180
﻿There are two more here.

01:25:24.680 --> 01:25:27.100
﻿﻿The cameraman and the reporter are with them!

01:25:27.600 --> 01:25:28.430
Damn...

01:25:29.010 --> 01:25:32.640
﻿Besides, I didn't come here to escape.

01:25:33.730 --> 01:25:35.480
﻿It was to lure you out.

01:25:36.150 --> 01:25:36.940
﻿What!?

01:25:37.610 --> 01:25:43.240
﻿Do you know why we carried out the hijack
﻿for the Buddha statues and not money?

01:25:44.410 --> 01:25:46.410
﻿In this information society...

01:25:46.410 --> 01:25:48.870
﻿It's only too easy to follow the money trail.

01:25:49.540 --> 01:25:54.000
﻿Thus, smuggling the priceless Buddha statues is comparatively safer.

01:25:54.960 --> 01:25:58.590
﻿Japanese Buddha statues are extremely popular overseas.

01:25:58.590 --> 01:26:00.380
﻿We've already secured a number of buyers.

01:26:02.170 --> 01:26:04.970
﻿Now that you've ruined my plan, allow me to return the favor!

01:26:09.640 --> 01:26:11.930
﻿We still have plenty of time.

01:26:12.470 --> 01:26:14.060
﻿Let's savor this while we can.

01:26:18.650 --> 01:26:19.820
﻿Hattori-kun!

01:26:19.820 --> 01:26:21.110
﻿You did a great job!

01:26:21.110 --> 01:26:22.190
﻿The credit goes to that boy.

01:26:22.820 --> 01:26:25.490
﻿That aside, is it possible to catch up with the airship?

01:26:25.490 --> 01:26:27.740
﻿I lost contact with him a moment ago.

01:26:28.200 --> 01:26:30.120
﻿I have a bad feeling about it.

01:26:30.120 --> 01:26:30.780
﻿Understood.

01:26:33.250 --> 01:26:34.580
﻿Listen up, Satoshi.

01:26:34.620 --> 01:26:35.920
﻿You should go home from here.

01:26:36.620 --> 01:26:37.210
﻿But...

01:26:37.670 --> 01:26:39.170
﻿I know.

01:26:39.170 --> 01:26:41.590
﻿We couldn't have protected the Buddha statues without your help.

01:26:42.760 --> 01:26:44.510
﻿﻿Hey, Uncle Heiji!

01:26:45.010 --> 01:26:47.890
﻿﻿I think the thieves' target is Goufuku Temple.

01:26:48.720 --> 01:26:50.850
﻿﻿There are many national treasures there.

01:26:51.260 --> 01:26:51.850
All right!

01:26:51.850 --> 01:26:52.600
﻿﻿Got it!

01:26:53.430 --> 01:26:54.770
﻿Then, just let me go with...

01:26:54.770 --> 01:26:55.230
﻿No way.

01:26:55.890 --> 01:26:57.230
﻿It's too dangerous.

01:26:57.230 --> 01:26:59.190
﻿Go home with Kazuha-neechan.

01:27:03.360 --> 01:27:05.780
﻿Satoshi-kun, let's do that, shall we?

01:27:06.610 --> 01:27:08.410
﻿Your mother must be very worried about you.

01:27:09.570 --> 01:27:10.620
﻿I know...

01:27:11.490 --> 01:27:14.620
﻿But, can I meet that kid called Conan-kun next time?

01:27:15.080 --> 01:27:18.000
﻿Uncle Heiji's going to save him, right?

01:27:18.000 --> 01:27:19.120
﻿Understood.

01:27:19.120 --> 01:27:19.750
﻿It's a promise!

01:27:20.670 --> 01:27:22.880
﻿Kazuha, I'll let you handle the rest.

01:27:22.880 --> 01:27:23.630
﻿Leave it to me!

01:27:24.090 --> 01:27:25.340
﻿Heiji, be careful.

01:27:26.880 --> 01:27:27.470
All right!

01:27:28.010 --> 01:27:28.970
﻿Let's get going.

01:27:46.990 --> 01:27:49.490
﻿To think that you were one of them!

01:27:50.910 --> 01:27:52.120
﻿OK on my end.

01:27:52.830 --> 01:27:54.120
﻿Hey...

01:27:54.620 --> 01:27:56.080
﻿Hurry up and untie us!

01:27:56.750 --> 01:27:58.620
﻿My bad, my bad.

01:27:58.620 --> 01:28:02.880
﻿I forgot to inform you that there's been a slight change of plans.

01:28:03.590 --> 01:28:04.300
﻿A change?

01:28:04.710 --> 01:28:07.840
﻿After all, the only loot left for us is this.

01:28:08.470 --> 01:28:10.220
﻿So you guys, along with the rest of them...

01:28:10.970 --> 01:28:12.140
Can just die.

01:28:12.510 --> 01:28:13.350
﻿What!?

01:28:27.440 --> 01:28:30.030
﻿Since this is the end, let me share something nice with you.

01:28:32.200 --> 01:28:37.290
﻿We'll be making our getaway on a cruiser parked near that bridge.

01:28:38.160 --> 01:28:40.660
﻿Immediately afterward, this airship will explode.

01:28:41.460 --> 01:28:43.630
﻿That includes the cabin housing the hostages.

01:28:44.170 --> 01:28:45.590
﻿Then, that's why you...

01:28:46.130 --> 01:28:51.220
﻿You may have managed to disarm the
﻿bombs planted on the fuel tanks, but...

01:28:51.220 --> 01:28:54.550
﻿There are actually two more in the cabin.

01:28:56.810 --> 01:28:57.390
Damn!

01:28:59.390 --> 01:29:00.930
﻿But before that...

01:29:04.440 --> 01:29:07.610
﻿I'll ensure you sink to the greatest depths of the sea!

01:29:08.730 --> 01:29:09.570
﻿﻿Damn it

01:29:09.570 --> 01:29:10.690
﻿What should I do?

01:29:10.940 --> 01:29:11.650
﻿﻿Something...

01:29:12.110 --> 01:29:16.240
﻿Isn't there something that can turn the tables?

01:29:23.580 --> 01:29:24.460
﻿We've caught up!

01:29:24.460 --> 01:29:25.130
﻿It's the airship!

01:29:25.670 --> 01:29:27.590
﻿They're flying really low.

01:29:28.550 --> 01:29:29.630
﻿Hey...

01:29:29.670 --> 01:29:31.050
﻿If they continue on that course...

01:29:31.050 --> 01:29:31.760
﻿Yeah...

01:29:31.760 --> 01:29:33.590
﻿They'll collide with the Akashi Kaikyou Bridge!

01:29:46.900 --> 01:29:48.610
﻿I can see Touto Tower!

01:29:48.610 --> 01:29:50.070
﻿And Rokkou's anchor mark too!

01:29:50.530 --> 01:29:51.320
﻿Amazing, amazing!

01:29:52.780 --> 01:29:57.280
﻿You think you can distract me and make
﻿me knock my head against the bridge?

01:29:57.780 --> 01:29:59.540
﻿As if I'd fall for something so childish.

01:30:18.640 --> 01:30:19.560
﻿What was that!?

01:30:19.560 --> 01:30:20.350
﻿What's happening!?

01:30:23.810 --> 01:30:25.140
Damn!

01:30:49.040 --> 01:30:49.840
﻿Amazing!

01:30:51.460 --> 01:30:52.880
﻿Just like a whale out of water!

01:31:20.410 --> 01:31:21.700
﻿Hello?

01:31:21.740 --> 01:31:24.200
﻿Hey Kudou, are you all right?

01:31:24.200 --> 01:31:26.660
﻿Hattori, just the right person for this.

01:31:26.660 --> 01:31:28.870
﻿Please contact the marine patrols.

01:31:28.870 --> 01:31:30.210
﻿Contact the marine patrols?

01:31:30.210 --> 01:31:32.500
﻿The mastermind, Fujioka, fell into the sea.

01:31:33.050 --> 01:31:35.050
﻿The culprit fell into the sea?

01:31:35.210 --> 01:31:35.590
﻿Oh, and...

01:31:36.550 --> 01:31:40.340
﻿﻿Their cruiser should be parked somewhere near the bridge.

01:31:40.340 --> 01:31:42.140
﻿﻿I'll leave their arrests to you.

01:31:42.140 --> 01:31:42.850
﻿All right, got it.

01:31:43.760 --> 01:31:45.100
﻿Well, I'll see you later.

01:31:45.100 --> 01:31:47.020
﻿I'll treat you to okonomiyaki tomorrow.

01:31:47.020 --> 01:31:48.480
﻿Look forward to it.

01:31:49.850 --> 01:31:51.060
﻿Hey, Hattori-kun.

01:31:52.400 --> 01:31:54.230
﻿Was that phone call to Kudou-kun?

01:31:55.780 --> 01:31:56.190
﻿Yeah...

01:31:57.780 --> 01:31:59.240
﻿I just wanted to ask, but...

01:32:00.110 --> 01:32:01.240
﻿Is Kudou-kun...

01:32:01.910 --> 01:32:02.910
﻿Actually Kaitou Kid?

01:32:07.910 --> 01:32:09.960
﻿Hey, everybody, you all right?

01:32:10.460 --> 01:32:11.960
﻿Yes, somehow.

01:32:11.960 --> 01:32:13.540
﻿Just a little shocked.

01:32:14.170 --> 01:32:15.800
﻿What happened to them?

01:32:15.800 --> 01:32:18.800
﻿If you're talking about the two culprits,
﻿I think they fell unconscious over there.

01:32:19.260 --> 01:32:23.050
﻿During the sudden climb just now
﻿they probably slammed into the wall.

01:32:23.050 --> 01:32:24.640
﻿Serves them right.

01:32:24.640 --> 01:32:27.350
﻿So we were saved because we were tied up?

01:32:29.690 --> 01:32:31.940
﻿Oh dear, what a surprise!

01:32:31.940 --> 01:32:36.110
﻿I wanted to survey the situation in the
﻿hall and the ship suddenly lurched.

01:32:36.690 --> 01:32:37.480
﻿Damn you, Kid!

01:32:37.990 --> 01:32:39.190
﻿Kid-sama!

01:32:39.190 --> 01:32:39.950
﻿Where's Conan-kun?

01:32:40.490 --> 01:32:42.910
﻿That boy is all right.

01:32:43.410 --> 01:32:45.200
﻿He should be here soon.

01:32:46.990 --> 01:32:49.790
﻿Well, please help untie everyone.

01:32:51.710 --> 01:32:53.250
﻿Kid-sama, mine too!

01:32:54.080 --> 01:32:55.210
﻿Wait, Kid!

01:32:55.250 --> 01:32:55.670
﻿Damn you!

01:32:55.670 --> 01:32:57.630
﻿Of course, please be so kind as to untie the fine inspector last.

01:33:05.640 --> 01:33:07.060
﻿Well, ladies and gentlemen...

01:33:07.060 --> 01:33:10.430
﻿As assured, the treasure has now become mine.

01:33:12.730 --> 01:33:13.440
﻿Wait!

01:33:13.440 --> 01:33:14.560
﻿Don't run, Kid!

01:33:14.560 --> 01:33:15.900
﻿Damn you, filthy thief!

01:33:16.770 --> 01:33:18.070
﻿It's "phantom thief."

01:33:32.250 --> 01:33:33.290
﻿And so are the bombs?

01:33:34.540 --> 01:33:36.290
﻿I see, got it.

01:33:36.290 --> 01:33:36.920
﻿Well done.

01:33:38.500 --> 01:33:39.630
﻿All the hostages are fine.

01:33:40.340 --> 01:33:42.920
﻿All the culprits have been apprehended.

01:33:45.390 --> 01:33:47.890
﻿And with that, we can close this case.

01:33:48.600 --> 01:33:49.390
﻿Yeah.

01:33:56.190 --> 01:33:57.940
﻿I'm so hungry!

01:34:01.320 --> 01:34:03.900
﻿It's finally time for our long awaited dinner!

01:34:03.900 --> 01:34:05.410
﻿I wonder if there'll be eel rice!

01:34:05.700 --> 01:34:08.120
﻿But, we seem to have forgotten something...

01:34:08.120 --> 01:34:09.120
﻿Now that you mention it...

01:34:14.000 --> 01:34:16.420
﻿And now, it's time for your long awaited quiz!

01:34:18.040 --> 01:34:19.500
﻿Nobody was waiting for that...

01:34:19.960 --> 01:34:24.760
﻿Ayumi-kun, Genta-kun and Mitsuhiko-kun are good children, but!

01:34:24.760 --> 01:34:28.930
﻿Who has something that has nothing to do with the airship?

01:34:33.060 --> 01:34:34.430
﻿That's... all of it?

01:34:34.980 --> 01:34:36.900
﻿Here's a hint if you don't know.

01:34:36.900 --> 01:34:39.190
﻿All three have something to do with it, don't they?

01:34:40.230 --> 01:34:45.280
﻿If the three of them are good children, that
﻿means they don't misbehave (hikoushinai), right?

01:34:45.280 --> 01:34:46.910
﻿Hikou-shinai...

01:34:46.910 --> 01:34:48.450
﻿Hikou-sen.

01:34:48.450 --> 01:34:49.370
It's an airship (hikousen).

01:34:50.030 --> 01:34:51.030
﻿That's it!

01:34:51.030 --> 01:34:51.620
﻿I see.

01:34:53.160 --> 01:34:56.960
﻿If only that guy were someone as simple as this riddle...

01:34:56.960 --> 01:35:00.630
﻿I would've caught him with ease and gotten printed on the front page!

01:35:03.590 --> 01:35:05.090
﻿Say, Sonoko-neechan...

01:35:05.550 --> 01:35:06.680
﻿Where's Ran-neechan?

01:35:07.840 --> 01:35:09.680
﻿Come to think of it, she's slow...

01:35:09.680 --> 01:35:13.060
﻿She asked me to come here first so I thought
﻿she must be going to the restroom, but...

01:35:13.850 --> 01:35:16.520
﻿She went up by the elevator.

01:35:17.350 --> 01:35:19.350
﻿Perhaps she went to see Kid?

01:35:19.860 --> 01:35:20.310
﻿What?

01:35:25.490 --> 01:35:27.110
﻿Guess there's no way light can go through...

01:35:30.200 --> 01:35:31.410
﻿Hey, Shinichi.

01:35:32.080 --> 01:35:34.370
﻿﻿Damn, I forgot all about that...

01:35:35.200 --> 01:35:36.790
﻿Yo, Ran.

01:35:36.790 --> 01:35:39.170
﻿It's been a pretty exciting day, huh?

01:35:40.420 --> 01:35:41.840
﻿Shinichi!

01:35:42.340 --> 01:35:44.050
﻿Please turn yourself in, Shinichi!

01:35:44.050 --> 01:35:46.670
﻿A thief is a thief after all, and it isn't a good thing!

01:35:47.010 --> 01:35:48.260
﻿Please, Shinichi!

01:35:55.720 --> 01:35:56.810
﻿I understand.

01:35:57.770 --> 01:35:58.980
﻿Then, you...

01:36:00.310 --> 01:36:04.230
﻿If you give me the treasure I long for most...

01:36:04.230 --> 01:36:06.070
﻿I'll turn myself in to the police.

01:36:07.030 --> 01:36:09.150
﻿But, I don't have anything...

01:36:10.860 --> 01:36:12.370
﻿It is, of course...

01:36:15.870 --> 01:36:16.450
﻿W-W-W-Wai...

